   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-154",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-154",
   "text": "Reinforcement Learning Your Way states that the complexity of state-of-the-art reinforcement-learning algorithms produces opacity that inhibits explainability and understanding. This independently corresponds to Kaal's broader critique of current explainable RL. The abstract does not establish Kaal's more specific claims about toy examples, user testing, visualization complexity, or open-source practice.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.3390/ai3020015"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4855607-013"
   },
   "sha256": "aace9b6bad1e03298ad4a3887892ba218244d7d9d86396b96588c76859dafcc4",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-153",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-153",
   "text": "AEGIS reports a literature gap: no systematic academic framework for recording, verifying, and ensuring accountability for organizational AI-agent actions. This supplies a direct accountability gap to which Kaal's immutable decision-and-transaction record is a proposed design response. The abstract does not validate blockchain recording or prove that no other framework exists outside the reviewed scope.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6392459"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5245185-033"
   },
   "sha256": "369c5d6a2a62135e07555db1a12a3d96334b9ced16c23e6718026c13fa48a264",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-152",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-152",
   "text": "Emergent Inter-Agent Conflict in Multi-Agent AI Systems identifies inter-agent objective divergence as a systems-level problem left largely outside human-AI alignment research. This extends Kaal's treatment of objective-function governance as a foundational policy problem into heterogeneous multi-agent interaction. The abstract proposition does not establish the frequency, severity, or institutional solution to divergence.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6853998"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6607458-030"
   },
   "sha256": "5ecaa494d3111bb9c4d7ae6af1c0585fa792193449a7f76a3397001c84ae3348",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-151",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-151",
   "text": "Agent-Based Trust and Reputation Model in Smart IoT Environments states that open, dynamic IoT environments require collaboration with unknown entities that lack a proven track record. This supplies a distinct machine-to-machine setting in which missing performance history is operationally salient, extending Kaal's generative-exchange track-record mechanism. It does not test generative distributions or establish that reputation alone makes IoT collaboration trustworthy.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.3390/technologies12110208"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6607458-012"
   },
   "sha256": "f603dc74d448ba89c777c068416d13e09d182038200d3fd82a17407442e33c76",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-150",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-150",
   "text": "Relational Integrity in Multi-Agent AI Systems argues that AI safety approaches which specify outcomes in advance become brittle when reality moves beyond the specification and can become sterile through over-constraint. This extends Kaal's brittleness mechanism for explicitly programmed legal expert systems to a broader AI-safety architecture setting. The abstract supplies an architectural claim, not a measured failure rate or evidence that every specified safety constraint is harmful.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6716459"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5541658-002"
   },
   "sha256": "05ec2fcf379c7b05eaa0373611566e897802e75dc0a813aebcf08c642fab627e",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-149",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-149",
   "text": "Performance rather than Reputation Affects Humans' Trust towards an Artificial Agent reports that stated agent reputation changes self-reported trust before interaction. This qualifies Kaal's trustworthiness mechanism by separating perceived trust induced by a reputation cue from trustworthy behavior produced by validated contribution and reputation-weighted incentives. The experiment does not test that incentive mechanism or show that pre-interaction trust predicts performance.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.31234/osf.io/h9urp"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6244278-027"
   },
   "sha256": "e1d84aec9987610eb4dc7afb6a5eb617fd959619ea484f126c075f2bbfee50a2",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-148",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-148",
   "text": "Bigdata-based university reputation measurement identifies electronic word of mouth as harder to measure, control, or influence than the factors used in traditional university rankings. This supplies a bounded university-reputation example of the objective-measurement difficulty in Kaal's reputation-governance claim. It does not show that university rankings allocate governance power or that any particular formula solves the problem.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.37380/jisib.v13i3.1112"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5254152-004"
   },
   "sha256": "bb19c0fe993d729042ceb8140d082c38cac1538f137d79f71b0167f001bd78ac",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-147",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-147",
   "text": "Algorithmic Reputation Equivalence reports that high human-perception reputation scores do not predict high AI decision-stage reputation scores and treats the two instruments as measuring categorically distinct phenomena. This provides a separate AI-facing example of why a single undifferentiated reputation measure can lose material information, extending Kaal's multidimensional-reputation requirement. It does not validate the WDAG design or transfer the brand-purchase result to dataset quality.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6887738"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5095633-033"
   },
   "sha256": "9644d9381a6008cd005893f99f80365e14d159c3a227e3d2e06054b1efca5c55",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-146",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-146",
   "text": "Towards Secure Embodied Communication Management in AI Era reports that end-to-end encryption and Byzantine consensus impose high overhead and require global coordination, making them impractical for time-sensitive exchange among resource-constrained embedded agents. This adds an operational limit to Kaal's separate warning that cryptography alone does not answer reputation-based exploits. The abstract does not test SPoS or establish that reputation guidance resolves the attacks.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.3390/s26092853"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5225296-030"
   },
   "sha256": "d6c6096736aef3eb3e5dac4d8edc54e9ef5268da749b07260e1e7915a9672d04",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-145",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-145",
   "text": "Private Credit and Bank Systemic Risk reports that 2026 BDC liquidity shocks were transmitted to banks mainly through credit agreements and increased systemic risk. This supplies a direct bank-exposure channel consistent with Kaal's account of fund shocks damaging financial institutions and the importance of bank lending exposure. The abstract does not establish that the same channel operates for every private-fund strategy.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.7138860"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2470008-006"
   },
   "sha256": "aa3038da1011da611454e4ea711d8809eed9f5866a11316a297a8355d90747b3",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-144",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-144",
   "text": "Litigation and Enforcement involving Private Funds after the Global Financial Crisis states that crisis-era disputes brought the private-fund legal and regulatory regime under closer scrutiny than in prior decades. This independently corresponds to Kaal's account of post-crisis private-fund scrutiny and a more demanding enforcement environment. The proposition does not measure enforcement intensity or prove that scrutiny improved outcomes.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.1093/law/9780198807247.003.0015"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2739479-015"
   },
   "sha256": "df490ddfd2bd589af8697e3c2a27c2d6958f595ec2f49accaf662504850a3e35",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-143",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-143",
   "text": "From Banks to Private Credit reports that private-credit expansion is closely linked to increased bank funding of private-credit vehicles, so regulation changes the location rather than the existence of credit risk. This supplies a bank–funding-network mechanism supporting Kaal's emphasis on regulated banks' exposure to private funds. The abstract does not concern credit derivatives specifically or quantify resulting systemic loss.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6800609"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2998097-009"
   },
   "sha256": "c83e840d20730f0cd80d77c8b326385121b3358451b4d4f5f165005b296bcb38",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-142",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-142",
   "text": "From Banks to Private Credit reports a 14-country panel association between tighter prudential regulation, constrained bank balance sheets, and significant private-credit growth. This independently corresponds to Kaal's account of post-crisis bank constraints creating room for private funds and alternative lenders. The abstract does not by itself establish causality or limit the expansion to SME finance.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6800609"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3002908-022"
   },
   "sha256": "dbde90016dde8c3fdf6b1b3f74b68aa9093afafbee6102b0da875b2048699e98",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-141",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-141",
   "text": "Market risk calculation for private equity fund-of-funds states that asset-level look-through is infeasible because the number of underlying assets makes it too costly and time-consuming. This supplies a portfolio-complexity mechanism consistent with Kaal's account of why managers can struggle to determine sensitive counterparty exposures. The abstract does not concern Form PF or show that benchmark estimates satisfy its reporting duty.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69554/gzgo2445"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2447306-003"
   },
   "sha256": "fbc4141cccdf9d2cbb5f9cdf105218937d2d6f80a3c4ca4135f70f513f1ba66d",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-140",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-140",
   "text": "Measuring Systemic Risk Contribution of International Mutual Funds states that the 2007–09 global financial crisis increased policy and academic attention to interconnected bank and nonbank systemic risk. This independently corresponds to Kaal's account of the crisis triggering a renewed wave of private-fund systemic-risk analysis. The proposition does not isolate private funds or establish their causal contribution to the crisis.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.1093/oso/9780198838104.003.0007"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2470008-007"
   },
   "sha256": "ba9f6c07129ac8111f723c4a906ca66a518631aaa11b31074f317731865246d3",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-139",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-139",
   "text": "Blinded by the Light identifies the assumption that more information is better as a major motivation for securities regulation. This states the regulatory premise that Kaal qualifies by showing why more disclosure may not improve governance when information is difficult to assess. The abstract proposition does not itself establish information overload or governance failure.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.413180"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-032"
   },
   "sha256": "6b49afe1ab36f4cbaedec37833e500e9c5df451456aa85e0bc67bd4e20815a8a",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-138",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-138",
   "text": "Digital Assets and Digital Inheritance states that digital inheritance by law or will can be limited by contract terms and constitutional privacy rights. This supplies succession-specific limits that qualify any uniform application of Kaal's property-style digital-object framework. The abstract does not identify which objects satisfy rivalry or resolve conflicts among license, service, confidentiality, and privacy rules.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.18254/s123456780015732-6"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5886342-015"
   },
   "sha256": "bf590e5e6dfd914e9e14477703fa1d3e7b5834cc8bebd584b23ac3fff61ab709",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-137",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-137",
   "text": "Digital Assets and Digital Inheritance states that only transferable digital assets pass by universal succession. This adds an inheritance-specific transferability condition to Kaal's property-style account of digital objects as rival digital information. The abstract does not adopt the Codex definition of rivalry or state how transferability is technically established.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.18254/s123456780015732-6"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5886342-015"
   },
   "sha256": "b3426aefd256bda1eb8f3225fe815cc2d8657070923d07eee327da59a2efaf2b",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-136",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-136",
   "text": "Collective Investment Management states that financial-stability objectives have come to shape the regime because collective investment management is associated with non-bank financial intermediation. This independently corresponds to Kaal's account of bank-like fund activity and liquidity transformation carrying financial-stability consequences. The abstract does not isolate hedge funds or quantify systemic risk.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.1093/law/9780198844877.003.0003"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2470008-010"
   },
   "sha256": "9ba324af83411e6f9601ab1e1fa078f7d0c651e02139d9bed09a09dc9703be67",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-135",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-135",
   "text": "Structuring Securities Regulation in the European Union predicts a domestic home bias in enforcement decisions that makes extraterritorial actions less likely and reduces incentives to comply. This supplies a countervailing under-enforcement risk to Kaal's warning against overbroad extraterritorial rule export. The abstract does not identify the optimal jurisdictional boundary or measure actual compliance effects.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.624582"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1664809-036"
   },
   "sha256": "79495d04ecd4684b91902e9b96a7e49665a960e53149bd461bce4fb40995485c",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-134",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-134",
   "text": "Intermediated Securities states that intermediation is essential to modern securities holding but imposes externalities on outside constituencies. This supplies a securities-market rationale for Kaal's account of decentralized exchanges removing third-party intermediation. The abstract does not establish that DEX trading is anonymous, secure, or free of different externalities.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.1093/law/9780198865858.003.0018"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808852-023"
   },
   "sha256": "f9e234e22ec25c6faa2b6f3294fca62253ab6acdb4bd08807435e45764c8121e",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-133",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-133",
   "text": "The regulation of Initial Coin Offerings states that the absence of regulation for ICOs and crypto-assets prompted regulators to move toward regulation. This supplies the regulatory-response arm of Kaal's legal-uncertainty account. The abstract does not establish that the SEC will declare ICOs illegal, identify the adopted rules, or measure the effect of the response.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.29053/pslr.v17i1.5092"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3067615-029"
   },
   "sha256": "71e601bbcdb423f7ebe56385d94b5b2fb8e6d3271c357c8f7a09d6e742302638",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-132",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-132",
   "text": "The regulation of Initial Coin Offerings states that ICO-driven market growth attracted investor capital despite information asymmetry and associated risks. This independently corresponds to Kaal's account of participation preceding mature reporting, accounting, and legal infrastructure. The abstract does not identify volatility magnitude or prove that information asymmetry caused the market growth.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.29053/pslr.v17i1.5092"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3067615-025"
   },
   "sha256": "39ac747efd8c7f90a039efc7724ab6b5f1ac69847528a512d6df0906b27e2930",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-131",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-131",
   "text": "The regulation of Initial Coin Offerings states that crypto-assets enabled token sales as an alternative way for emerging businesses to raise capital through ICOs. This independently supports the alternative-funding-channel component of Kaal's ICO claim. The abstract does not show that ICOs overtook venture capital, quantify proceeds, or establish comparative efficiency.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.29053/pslr.v17i1.5092"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3002908-039"
   },
   "sha256": "691594349b66689aa3a5854921688cc6237a16213e2651b92bb9a395795508a7",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-130",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-130",
   "text": "Capital Regulation for Position Risk in Banks, Securities Firms, and Insurance Companies concludes that market forces, rather than minimum regulatory capital requirements, dominate capital decisions at most leading firms. This supports the importance of market discipline in Kaal's Basel account while qualifying any reading that formal minima alone drive practice. The source does not isolate hedge-fund exposures, internal ratings, disclosure, or leverage effects.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.1093/acprof:oso/9780195169713.003.0001"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405660-034"
   },
   "sha256": "6a491aac98d2b1c93787d21a205a62629d84cd635ca2f84fce082718704babc9",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-129",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-129",
   "text": "Quantum-Resistant Cryptography states that large-scale quantum computers threaten to make traditional cryptography protecting online banking, secure communications, and digital-asset transfers obsolete. This independently corresponds to Kaal's quantum-threat and quantum-safe-transition claims. The abstract states a prospective risk and does not establish a deployment date or that every current protocol fails identically.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.4018/979-8-3373-1370-2.ch004"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4900880-006"
   },
   "sha256": "804be78f1ca5ff1fa3d5191797aa10b5e545a56c545069b1ff8c0736e8135648",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-128",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-128",
   "text": "The Qualification of Crypto-Assets as Securities Under Turkish Law states that Turkish law has no published guidance on when crypto-assets qualify as securities. This supplies a comparative guidance gap relevant to Kaal's rights-based classification account under German law. The source does not establish that German criteria control in Turkey or state the classification rule Turkish authorities should adopt.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69800/blr.1838778"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3117224-028"
   },
   "sha256": "c16ab51ede5499a7ad2732aafe7cb76d54110bf3f45424f640f6a039c59798cd",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-127",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-127",
   "text": "Four Predictions About the Future of EU Securities Regulation concludes that the proposed process will fail because it does not address national protectionism and bureaucratic inertia. This independently corresponds to Kaal's national-protectionism barrier to cross-jurisdiction harmonization. The source concerns a broader EU process and does not specifically test close-out netting or documentation standards.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.376720"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2998097-007"
   },
   "sha256": "1acbb254d19f0c1949274d358a0c59635f3c6293bd0997d7ab72ba1adb854cb9",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-126",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-126",
   "text": "MiFID II and EMIL: The impact of regulation on securities operations in European markets reports that financial institutions increasingly say industry change will occur only through regulation and that buy-side firms are proposing a regulatory approach. This independently corresponds to Kaal's account of regulation as an endogenous cause of market change. The abstract does not establish that dynamic regulation is the preferred response or measure the resulting changes.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69554/zfut4128"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2273857-012"
   },
   "sha256": "88f7b60b36afc829e27a549a522bac263b25e3c43365501021a19432f18d187a",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-125",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-125",
   "text": "Legal regulation of digital financial assets in Russia recommends adding a legal definition of cryptocurrency system and a classification of digital currency to Federal Law 259-FZ. This independently identifies the definition-and-classification design problem to which Kaal's broad digital-asset definition responds. The abstract does not endorse Kaal's definition or specify the categories the Russian law should adopt.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.54217/2588-0136.2023.37.3.015"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3606663-004"
   },
   "sha256": "92ed6015584542d8c4859ec083b92c55745a59cd6d3ab83483e8c95544a28d99",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-124",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-124",
   "text": "Legal regulation of digital assets exchanges: on the example of Binance states that Binance's operations substantially influence the development of global norms for digital-asset exchanges. This supplies a concrete exchange-level instance of Kaal's account of centralized technology firms retaining norm-setting power. The abstract does not show that Binance's influence is untraceable, exclusive, or effective across all jurisdictions.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.46914/2959-4197-2024-1-4-44-51"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3709041-026"
   },
   "sha256": "e9607e142505c1249dd86da3e1795094572eebbcff5627a7f72b0ca59eea27ad",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-123",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-123",
   "text": "Regulation, Supervision, and Oversight identifies weaknesses in securities holding and settlement infrastructure as a potential source of systemic disturbances. This supplies the baseline settlement-infrastructure risk mechanism to which Kaal's settlement-speed claims respond. The abstract does not show that sub-ten-second settlement eliminates counterparty or systemic risk.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.1093/law/9780192855510.003.0009"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411110-014"
   },
   "sha256": "cba4d9f8f2e0e5c3063d3617bfcd25c9b124bc909478f248fc3960225f5879eb",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-122",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-122",
   "text": "Digital Transformation in securities services: The BNP Paribas case study states that multidisciplinary use of AI, blockchain, and data could generate operational efficiencies and synergies. This supplies a proposed efficiency mechanism relevant to Kaal's observations about lower fees among advisers using the same technologies. The abstract provides no fee comparison and does not establish that efficiencies are passed through to investors.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69554/wgyh7802"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2998033-030"
   },
   "sha256": "b2a7893bec18ca2820f563a186d38dec6fdcb228266127de9dd8d470f7ea95ff",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-121",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-121",
   "text": "The Role of Self-Regulation in Supporting Korea's Securities Markets defines self-regulation broadly across listed-company quality, disclosure, governance, broker-dealer, trading, and exchange-organization rules. This supplies a concrete institutional inventory for Kaal's mixed mandatory-rule, market-solution, and private-ordering design. The abstract does not measure adaptive capacity, collective-action effects, or regulatory-cycle dampening.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.293565"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2273857-066"
   },
   "sha256": "0465f7959aebbf789ce79f98c6566f98c160addcf23db1564a3c60c2fd33394c",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-120",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-120",
   "text": "What you need to know about the new Securities Financing Transaction Regulation reports that the 2008-2009 recession was followed by substantial regulatory change in European financial markets. This independently supplies the crisis-to-governance-adjustment arm of Kaal's regulatory sine curve. The abstract does not address the later relaxation, revision, or retraction arm.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69554/pdjm7590"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2273857-028"
   },
   "sha256": "2e5586750aaca0ca11d91cdc3e993b7c9eb5600e9e87949bf5e5ac02f39e2f7a",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-119",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-119",
   "text": "Digital Financial Assets: Problems and Prospects of Legal Regulation states that the emergence and diffusion of digital assets, especially cryptocurrencies, necessitated legal regulation. This independently corresponds to Kaal's technology-use-to-legal-adaptation mechanism. The abstract does not identify the timing of the lag, the adequacy of the response, or the design every jurisdiction should adopt.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.17803/1994-1471.2020.115.6.043-054"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227933-024"
   },
   "sha256": "533400db21164ec2f6272adec8850272e075ef7cc857428f172d275d0a17d81d",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-118",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-118",
   "text": "Digital assets, personal property and categorisation states that digital assets disrupt the traditional two-category classification of personal property. This identifies the classification problem to which Kaal's definition of a Digital Object as rival digital information supplies a proposed property-style response. The source does not endorse that definition or establish that rivalry resolves every property question.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.1017/lst.2026.10116"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5886342-015"
   },
   "sha256": "169fbb2906c60db53262e6a97b1cadf7b901f7a3252c308c18da2d8e9d14d434",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-117",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-117",
   "text": "Legal regulation of taxation of transactions with digital (virtual) assets argues that rapid market growth necessitates international harmonization of tax policies. This is a tax-specific contrary position to Kaal's broader account of harmonization as only a partial and potentially unsustainable answer. The abstract does not compare alternative tax designs or show that harmonization remains current as technology changes.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.37634/efp.2024.10.6"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5554218-011"
   },
   "sha256": "1ca5aaba6687e7037702582a4c9e4e360c900c4f7d6ef3bc792935296906476a",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-116",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-116",
   "text": "Comment, Regulation and Investors' Trust in the Securities Markets states that regulation relaxes when market prices rise and becomes stricter when prices fall. This independently corresponds to Kaal's historical account of regulatory expansion and relaxation and the regulatory sine curve. The abstract does not identify the causal political-economy variables or establish that every market follows this cycle.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.333340"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1998455-025"
   },
   "sha256": "f7a04b05aad829f3ad49d1e3111335dc922a9604ca426dd9f872d1f6a9414236",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-115",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-115",
   "text": "Digital Financial Assets: Segments and Prospects of Legal Regulation in the BRICS Countries states that the absence of legal regulation may give rise to illegal asset turnover and fraud. This independently corresponds to Kaal's regulatory-oversight-to-fraud-risk mechanism. The abstract states possibility rather than measured incidence or causation.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.21684/2412-2343-2019-6-4-95-113"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4900878-020"
   },
   "sha256": "def14513e7ddc0640a75d4e462ba3853a4a4a7ba72346f655ca7ed334bc0f519",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-114",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-114",
   "text": "Digital Financial Assets: Segments and Prospects of Legal Regulation in the BRICS Countries reports that digital financial assets were already circulating in some countries before legal regulation existed. This independently corresponds to Kaal's technology-use-before-legal-adaptation mechanism. The abstract does not establish the duration of the lag or that every jurisdiction must adopt the same legal response.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.21684/2412-2343-2019-6-4-95-113"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227933-024"
   },
   "sha256": "c15b7a435d75453124dcfbbf9f53536e8b8164034ab1494b0745d25ba6d3f4ae",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-113",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-113",
   "text": "Cat Food Communists and the Politics of Securities Regulation states that SEC v. Ralston Purina requires investor sophistication and access to information for a securities sale to qualify as a private offering. This supplies a judicial eligibility test relevant to Kaal's account of private-placement investor limits. It does not establish that accredited-investor or qualified-purchaser status alone satisfies the test or supplies adequate protection.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6252878"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2811729-016"
   },
   "sha256": "b54de6a9cd5ce8bf7f5a9787b8c523d1c8dc1f6cf5d3f616ba7b315c98ab3dae",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-112",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-112",
   "text": "Digital Financial Assets: Problems and Prospects of Legal Regulation reports increasingly frequent social use of digital assets as a means of payment. This supplies jurisdiction-specific evidence for the transaction-use premise in Kaal's liquidity claim. The abstract does not measure market liquidity or establish that payment use causes liquidity to increase.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.34925/eip.2024.174.1.094"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4033886-030"
   },
   "sha256": "a53214816b4fdcff9ad5b7c2bcaf76200cb9d9d7e506effa41fa0cf58a785464",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-111",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-111",
   "text": "PSD3 and the Regulation on Payment Services in the Context of Crypto Assets identifies MiCA electronic-money tokens and asset-referenced tokens as stablecoin categories characterized by a payment function. This adds a use-oriented regulatory classification to Kaal's broad digital-asset taxonomy. The abstract does not establish that every stablecoin functions as payment or that these categories exhaust stablecoin designs.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-74889-9_16"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3606663-004"
   },
   "sha256": "c0ed583d1bb41a41f8d00159a70a4ca87c9ae65fbc0dde96d7a2881d11d53424",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-110",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-110",
   "text": "The case for self-regulation for the digital assets industry reports that self-regulation and SROs have been incorporated into legal frameworks to support effective and efficient capital-market development. This is institutionally consistent with Kaal's mixed mandatory-rule, market-solution, and private-ordering design. The abstract proposition does not measure adaptive capacity, collective-action effects, or regulatory-cycle dampening.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69554/pgjq5722"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2273857-066"
   },
   "sha256": "941a4ca791473e4eb6e8ca53f31bd10778325fea15a043a352627367b12b9f94",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-109",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-109",
   "text": "Avoiding the Anticommons Tragedy in Canadian Securities Regulation concludes that nationalization or harmonization could increase Canadian securities business by lowering firm-level costs. This is a jurisdiction-specific counterpoint to Kaal's claims that jurisdictional competition adapts faster and harmonization can select the wrong rule. The abstract does not compare adaptability over time or establish that harmonization is generally superior.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.327221"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2029983-006"
   },
   "sha256": "516132dbd0937ad4ebc4f20cd5748e41afce0bd9ce8511b49cb57e1794cad520",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-108",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-108",
   "text": "Avoiding the Anticommons Tragedy in Canadian Securities Regulation attributes higher regulatory costs to provincial regulators that fail to internalize the effects of their actions on the wider market. This supplies a concrete negative externality that qualifies Kaal's account of competition between legislators as a quality-sensitive feedback mechanism. The abstract does not show that all jurisdictional competition produces an anticommons.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.327221"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2267560-030"
   },
   "sha256": "f47b4cd0748531a4647fc73f3248142e727e7c4c79198c8bb0ff4b7508d5415e",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-107",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-107",
   "text": "Valuing illiquid and ‘hard to value’ assets defines fair value as the price obtainable in an orderly transaction between market participants and identifies it as the reporting basis at discrete times. This supplies the benchmark relevant to Kaal's warning that thin-market exchange quotes may not indicate contemporaneous fair market value. The abstract does not establish which valuation inputs are reliable for every illiquid asset.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69554/ffvl2175"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-013"
   },
   "sha256": "66c3e14b1b401187ed416fa1d919763f30bfdada2516d13128f17bbcdb5a3f64",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-106",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-106",
   "text": "The Market of Digital Financial Assets and the Stock Market of Ukraine identifies five integration directions: tokenization of financial instruments, DLT post-trading, custody infrastructure, investor access, and regulatory compatibility. These independently correspond to Kaal's tokenization-access, ledger-settlement, and custody-infrastructure mechanisms. The abstract identifies directions, not implemented or measured effects.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.32782/city-development.2026.2-22"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4900878-037"
   },
   "sha256": "bae517ce8d0d0f5e0915b8b9c7b65e1fd8ece3ca9d2ffad4f7f7dc5fbc7f3837",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-105",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-105",
   "text": "Prospects for introducing the concept of digital things and digital content reports that Ukraine ranked third in cryptocurrency use despite lacking a legal framework. This qualifies any reading of Kaal's legal-certainty mechanism as necessary for all forms of adoption. It does not address durable market confidence, compliant custody, or mainstream institutional participation.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.15804/ksm20230201"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3936876-001"
   },
   "sha256": "b6933b993e9c470af2681c8c3c967575ed86b6eda25a6d01cea7c2379edbce74",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-104",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-104",
   "text": "Commercial Law: Corporate Law, Securities Regulation, and Antitrust reports that irrational behavior persists even in well-functioning competitive markets. This independently supports the bounded-rationality premise in Kaal's investor-protection claim. The abstract does not specifically address professional investors, complex instruments, or hard-to-value assets.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.1093/oso/9780190901349.003.0011"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-037"
   },
   "sha256": "e35abd29e4bb17707a35f149004b57587acded75865ac5c31971e3f3701de4f0",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-103",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-103",
   "text": "Digital financial assets and digital currency: legal nature and legal regulation of turnover states that absent regulation produces non-uniform enforcement and unpredictable legal relations. This identifies a cost of regulatory gaps that qualifies Kaal's critique of uniform digital-asset rules and corresponds to his view that existing initiatives remain partial. It does not show that comprehensive uniformity is feasible or preferable.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.1051/shsconf/202110602005"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5554218-013"
   },
   "sha256": "8cbf3a4726f54f5a6f6be130239bfc07e2743f29e125184d0ba7c21c0ca6aaec",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-102",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-102",
   "text": "Crypto-assets: Crossing the chasm? locates crypto-assets' novelty in the distributed character of blockchain networks rather than in their investment characteristics. This independently corresponds to Kaal's distributed-validation mechanism. The abstract does not establish disintermediation or performance effects in any particular market.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69554/xmbt7179"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3002908-015"
   },
   "sha256": "ebfeac52d6a0067c0084c323fc9a1c0540510aebcecf56251a97b80a2089315b",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-101",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-101",
   "text": "Legal Regulation of Transactions with Digital Financial Assets reports that these assets became widespread after Russia recognized digital rights in civil law and adopted a special transaction law. This sequence is consistent with Kaal's legal-certainty-to-market-confidence mechanism. The abstract does not establish causation, investor confidence, or mainstream institutional adoption.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.25683/volbi.2022.61.469"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3936876-001"
   },
   "sha256": "3b85c61b60980475936331f5a6ee3ae90bba1924c456cfa62a4da0d5d76439a7",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-100",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-100",
   "text": "Self-Regulation and Securities Markets states that exchanges have a liquidity-based incentive to regulate insider trading and manipulation. This supplies a traditional-market incentive mechanism relevant to Kaal's identification of market-integrity risks on decentralized exchanges. It does not establish that decentralized exchanges possess or effectively exercise the same self-regulatory incentive.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.318939"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808852-029"
   },
   "sha256": "6fd2667c7513ea73f213e250ef8117ff229817ce834b7931a7bb8bbd30aaffd7",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-099",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-099",
   "text": "Digital asset adoption: Technology and regulation are ready — conviction remains the final hurdle states that cryptographic standards and operational frameworks underpin secure custody. This independently complements Kaal's requirement for enhanced digital-asset custody security infrastructure. The abstract does not identify particular controls or test their effectiveness.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69554/ztbo2722"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3936876-028"
   },
   "sha256": "38f41f90c9bc8ba886b8ceeccdad4c5c5f3a633263009b38c6d7439c81734d48",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-098",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-098",
   "text": "The Legal Recognition and Regulation of Digital Assets links the cross-border and decentralized character of digital assets to legal uncertainty, regulatory fragmentation, and enforcement difficulty. This independently corresponds to Kaal's cross-jurisdictional uncertainty mechanism. It does not prove regulatory arbitrage or establish that uniform law is the appropriate remedy.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.54097/ybywwm42"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5554218-027"
   },
   "sha256": "ef4b22fc6213095660edf0a4cf5faa87f2ac8736167db6e3785ab441578a9897",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-097",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-097",
   "text": "Risk of digital assets: Developments in regulation and implementation reports that some blockchain implementations trend toward centralization and enable new intermediaries. This independently corresponds to Kaal's recentralization mechanism. The abstract concerns digital-asset systems, not AI governance, and does not establish that all blockchain networks recentralize.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69554/qpvt8533"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4796714-012"
   },
   "sha256": "22ebb81a3f87c0d1b3474a2fd421ac9f4f654d9deed572ab605f1250d0485019",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-096",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-096",
   "text": "The securities financing transaction regulation characterizes SFTR as a huge data-gathering exercise for securities-lending participants. This independently corresponds to the scale component of Kaal's reporting-burden claim. The abstract does not identify pre-screening, staffing, transaction costs, or hedge-fund-specific effects.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69554/pjlr5811"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-034"
   },
   "sha256": "d1b5852dbdf8852d4f6e7905b4fb8504ae18d19c865ed1f0ec346ba34b47f156",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-095",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-095",
   "text": "Legal Regulation of the Issue of Digital Financial Assets identifies the absence of a uniform approach to digital-law and digital-financial-asset concepts in Russian doctrine and enforcement practice. This independently supplies a jurisdiction-specific classification inconsistency corresponding to Kaal's classification-problem mechanism. It does not establish that the inconsistency caused regulatory failure or that uniformity is normatively preferable.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.61205/jrp.2023.094"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2740477-008"
   },
   "sha256": "5a6556e02e0dcd27920daec378c9c899bce4d44125cc7fdbdbad39b9f3b3af75",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-094",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-094",
   "text": "Cryptocurrency Digital Assets reports no significant risk-adjusted return difference between FANG stocks and Bitcoin. This supplies evidence of similarity on one performance dimension corresponding to Kaal's observation that stocks and cryptocurrencies can appear similar. It does not address the abuse, legal, acceptance, or use differences on which Kaal's regulatory distinction rests.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.33423/jaf.v23i2.6090"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4033886-018"
   },
   "sha256": "bab27d1a5602f10f80e2ca3ac4026c2fb0ac9737a046b96b56884eb4ce8d9ab0",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-093",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-093",
   "text": "The Quantum Clock Is Ticking reports resource estimates indicating that elliptic-curve cryptography used by major blockchains may be breakable with fewer quantum resources than previously believed. This independently supplies a concrete threat mechanism corresponding to Kaal's requirement for quantum-resistant cryptography. The abstract does not show that any blockchain has been broken or independently validate the estimates beyond its reported method.",
   "responseType": "qualification",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.7176419"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4900878-034"
   },
   "sha256": "393df6d7d8e993fea2a05a22312d16cd76b446f6785773a9ce5cf8d7afc32d90",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level qualification",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-092",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-092",
   "text": "Tokenisation: Assembling the building blocks of an institutional digital assets marketplace predicts that tokenising assets will reduce issuance, servicing, and ownership-transfer frictions and remove access barriers to capital markets. This independently corresponds to Kaal's tokenisation-access mechanism. It is a long-term forecast, not an observed result, and does not establish fractional ownership.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69554/nqxw4595"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4900878-037"
   },
   "sha256": "9ba2bc96cd7b43518f72045659ee20dd0fd888d1438f132317ab393294d8c67e",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-091",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-091",
   "text": "Analyzing the Legal and Policy Implications of the Investment and Securities Act 2025 on Digital Assets Offering Platforms states that Nigeria's Investments and Securities Act 2025 officially recognizes digital assets as securities. This supplies a Nigerian legislative example corresponding to Kaal's proposal for legal recognition of digital securities. It does not establish the effectiveness or content of U.S.-specific trading and margining reforms.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6758718"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411110-024"
   },
   "sha256": "5d57a174e24d3424dbfbaa986d99e15cd391d5351e72d8dd9682a95dc832e8e5",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-090",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-090",
   "text": "Opportunities in digital assets and digital custody states that adoption of digital assets necessitates a transformation of custody comparable to securities dematerialization. This independently corresponds to Kaal's claim that reliable custody infrastructure is a condition for institutional adoption. The abstract does not identify investor behavior or validate a particular custody solution.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69554/vhtu7103"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3936876-022"
   },
   "sha256": "710981368d14abeed2ece31eba47e9773080893136bc2faf3885f772867acbe2",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level agreement",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-089",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-089",
   "text": "Legal regulation of digital financial assets – requirements for the transfer of securities of a business entity states that Russian Federal Law on Digital Financial Assets recognizes a digital right requiring transfer of equity securities. This supplies a jurisdiction-specific legislative example corresponding to Kaal's proposal to recognize digital securities. It does not establish equivalence to the proposed U.S. trading or margining reforms.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.52468/2542-1514.2025.9(3).124-133"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411110-024"
   },
   "sha256": "de7e7484e2535ff3b4228f8763ea6e0bec76b4c3ba1d136c0a3e757cdc9f883e",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "substantively reviewed abstract-level extension",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.62,
   "mappingAmbiguous": false
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-08-08-088",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-08-08-088",
   "text": "Digital and crypto-assets: Tracking global adoption rates and impacts on securities services states that tokenisation can release trapped liquidity and open markets for otherwise untradeable asset classes. This independently corresponds to Kaal's tokenisation-liquidity-access mechanism. The abstract does not establish fractional ownership, adoption, or measured market performance.",
   "responseType": "agreement",
   "datePublished": "2026-08-08",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://doi.org/10.69554/rzil3872"
   },
   "extends": {
    "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4900878-037"
   },
   "sha256": "d8d357e481a5e99375ef7db5757b0a24c74e89c09d876c0a14977efe752b072f",
   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
