  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-993",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-993",
   "text": "The impact of regulatory lag on holding period returns of common stockholders of electric utilities should be assessed against Kaal's source-bound claim that The fourth Howey prong fails because LER accrual is automated by smart contract and driven by the shareholder's own decision to keep holding, leaving the issuer's role ministerial rather than entrepreneurial. The current metadata indicates a plausible connection through regulatory lag, but the defensible response is a qualification until the source text confirms agreement, scope, methods, and limitations.",
