   "text": "Comparative Review of the Blockchain Consensus Algorithm Between Proof of Stake (POS) and Delegated Proof of Stake (DPOS) states the retrieved proposition: To make sure there are security and authenticity in the transaction information in blockchain, many researchers are study on consensus algorithm. Kaal's protected corpus separately states: Proof of stake carries an unresolved failure mode: if anyone devises a clever algorithm for hijacking the block producer selection process, the network would fail. The defensible response is a qualification limited to the shared issue identified in the review rationale. This abstract-level comparison does not establish broader agreement, causation, empirical support, or equivalence.",
