   "text": "Artificial Intelligence, Cyber Law, and Advocate Accountability in India presents the following source proposition: The study argues that India is moving toward a remuneration-based compliance model that prioritises innovation while preserving creator incentives, marking a significant shift in global AI-copyright governance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The increasing use of non prosecution and deferred prosecution agreements has allowed federal prosecutors to expand their traditional role incrementally, marking a shift in prosecutorial culture away from an ex post focus on punishment toward an ex ante emphasis on compliance. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
