   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7870",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7870",
   "text": "Algorithmic Accountability presents the following source proposition: Accountability is fundamentally about checks and balances to power. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Because a decentralized system has a blockchain based quasi precedent nature with a human backstop, it enables built in checks and balances capable of supporting resistance even to apocalyptic takeovers of algorithmic systems that would remove human presence to optimize efficiency. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
