   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7867",
   "text": "&amp;nbsp;Prompt Accountability and Session-Context Disclosure presents the following source proposition: It is field-sourced conceptual work with external literature support. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Private foundations exercise plutocratic power because their leaders and trustees are not elected democratically, they are permitted to operate in perpetuity, and their operations lack accountability and transparency. The proposed response is an agreement: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
