  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7863",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7863",
   "text": "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Corporate Governance and Executive Accountability: The Broader Relevance of Enhanced Accountability Measures in the Financial Sector&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; presents the following source proposition: This article highlights an important development in the financial sector which it argues should be given greater prominence in this discourse. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Contingent convertible bonds placed in executive compensation serve a different purpose than those sold to investors: the point is not capital infusion during a crisis but governance-improving design that optimizes management incentives. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
