  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7855",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7855",
   "text": "Discretionary Disclosure, Transparency, and Accountability presents the following source proposition: Using a game-theoretic model, I explore how this discretion affects political accountability and policy-making incentives. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Automatic adjustment mechanisms trade democratic input for responsiveness: by removing policy changes from the legislative agenda they limit opportunities for public debate and scrutiny, which raises accountability and transparency concerns. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
