   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7854",
   "text": "Discretionary Disclosure, Transparency, and Accountability presents the following source proposition: Politicians often have the discretion to conceal politically relevant information since disclosure is not mandatory. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Private foundations exercise plutocratic power because their leaders and trustees are not elected democratically, they are permitted to operate in perpetuity, and their operations lack accountability and transparency. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
