   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7853",
   "text": "Accountability and Responsibility in Corporate Governance presents the following source proposition: But it is still not clear precisely where to draw the line between accountability and responsibility. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Contractual consent to a cash out does not extinguish fiduciary claims: a minority shareholder who agreed to receive cash for shares may still challenge the merger as a breach of fiduciary duty. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
