  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7851",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7851",
   "text": "Accountability and Responsibility in Corporate Governance presents the following source proposition: A major problem of modern corporate governance is how to reconcile making corporate managers more accountable to shareholders with ensuring that managers respond to society's needs. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Reforms that increase executive accountability to shareholders and increase shareholder control over executives do not solve the problem of corporate short-term focus. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
