  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7847",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7847",
   "text": "Discretionary Disclosure and Political Accountability presents the following source proposition: The core of analysis identifies a trade-off between a detection-based mechanism under mandatory disclosure and an inference-based mechanism under discretionary disclosure. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The strong trust that sustained Maghribi trade, in which embezzlement was rare despite extreme information asymmetry, cannot be explained by a strong centralized government, since the Maghribis could not form a centralized legal or political hierarchy and the official legal channels were slow and unreliable. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
