   "mappingConfidence": 0.4145,
   "mappingAmbiguous": true
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7842",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7842",
   "text": "Doing Just Enough? presents the following source proposition: This chapter demonstrates that the theory of quasi-compliance is a useful framework for understanding post-atrocity governments' reactions to international pressure for accountability. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The SEC's efforts to clarify and optimize the post Dodd-Frank framework cut both ways: they supported industry compliance with the revised standards while simultaneously creating uncertainty and higher costs for the industry. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
