   "text": "Framing and overflowing of public sector accountability innovations presents the following source proposition: Findings The accountability reports became bureaucratic communications between the reporting and central agencies. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Although aggregate venture capital sector data arguably only confirms what media reporting already showed for 2005 to 2015, the venture capital data, especially examined granularly, may provide earlier signals for regulators to identify areas of prospective regulatory need. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
