   "text": "Internal control, accountability and corporate governance presents the following source proposition: Stewardship and personal accountability are found to be the core elements of medieval internal control. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Reforms that increase executive accountability to shareholders and increase shareholder control over executives do not solve the problem of corporate short-term focus. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
