   "text": "Understanding accountability in blockchain systems presents the following source proposition: Design/methodology/approach This study draws on theorising in the accountability literature to study how blockchains relate to our construction and understanding of accountability. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Existing blockchains and DAOs still lack genuine decentralization, and there are currently no true DAOs: Bitcoin's proof of work protocol has produced mining pools because of economies of scale and unbalanced reward structures. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
