   "text": "Accountability in Health Care presents the following source proposition: The debate on accountability within the public sector has been lively in the past decade. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Because CIAs have so far been used predominantly in the health care industry, and because that industry has a public or quasi-public good character, the application of CIAs outside health care could be limited, and without broader application their impact on corporate law may be limited as well. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
