   "text": "KnowLedger - A Multi-Agent System Blockchain for Smart Cities Data presents the following source proposition: Hence, solutions are required where data may be committed by any actor, being, at the same time, freely available to the community. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Because blockchain guarantees prevent any participant from circumventing the coded set of governance rules, a lower level of oversight and monitoring of agents is needed, which changes the cost structure of the principal agent relationship. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
