   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7740",
   "text": "A Multidimensional Environment Implementation for Enhancing Agent Interaction presents the following source proposition: Each of them has its own process and rules to support agents' interaction. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Because each AI interaction is episodic and each evaluation ephemeral, an agent that performs brilliantly across a thousand consecutive tasks has no mechanism by which that track record reshapes its subsequent behavior, unlike a human professional whose accumulated successes and failures shape judgment. The proposed response is an agreement: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
