   "text": "Model based approach to detect emergent behavior in multi-agent systems presents the following source proposition: In MAS, agents are usually designed with distribution of functionality and control. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Because each AI interaction is episodic and each evaluation ephemeral, an agent that performs brilliantly across a thousand consecutive tasks has no mechanism by which that track record reshapes its subsequent behavior, unlike a human professional whose accumulated successes and failures shape judgment. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
