   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7735",
   "text": "Multi-Agent Orchestration in Enterprise CRM: Agentforce Frameworks for Autonomous Service Delivery presents the following source proposition: The analysis highlights improvements in scalability, decision quality, and operational efficiency, while also addressing governance, interoperability, and policy compliance challenges. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Decentralized data production will succeed only if it solves fraudulent submissions, content moderation, and alignment with ethical and legal frameworks; these are necessary conditions, not incidental risks. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
