   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7697",
   "text": "Dynamic protocols for open agent systems presents the following source proposition: Moreover, there is no support for run-time specification modification. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The possibility loop is generatively open: each completed cycle leaves the system with a strictly enlarged action space, because a successful proposal adds a job specification, tag, or template that did not previously exist. The proposed response is an agreement: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
