   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7696",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7696",
   "text": "LEGAL ACCOUNTABILITY OF AUTONOMOUS AI SYSTEMS IN CRIMINAL JUSTICE presents the following source proposition: When an AI system takes an action that is normally a crime if taken by a human being, it becomes far less clear as to how to impose liability under law. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Existing corporate criminal liability combined with the absence of clear Department of Justice standards for charging businesses can push organizations to adopt unproven compliance programs and generate other inefficiencies. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
