   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7695",
   "text": "&lt;span&gt;CRI: A Multi-Factor Reputation System for Autonomous Agent Commerce&lt;/span&gt; presents the following source proposition: Each component is grounded in published research from trust systems, game theory, and commons governance. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Truly increasing counterparty trust in decentralized smart contract based commerce requires that counterparties be able to review a long history of each other's conduct in decentralized commerce and of performance in earlier smart contracts. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
