   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7690",
   "text": "Autonomous QA Agent: A Retrieval-Augmented Framework for Reliable Selenium Script Generation presents the following source proposition: While Large Language Models (LLMs) can generate code, they often hallucinate non-existent UI elements. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Retrieval-augmented generation reduces but does not eliminate hallucination: leading legal research tools including Lexis+AI and Westlaw AI-Assisted Research still generate false citations or facts in 17 to 33 percent of cases. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
