   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7685",
   "text": "The Rise of the Agent Economy: Autonomous Agent Organizations as a New Form of Economic Infrastructure presents the following source proposition: The concept of Autonomous Agent Organizations (AAOs) is introduced as a functional subclass of Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs), distinguished by their greater economic autonomy and composable inter-agent collaboration. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Decentralized Autonomous Organizations challenge the core belief that governance necessitates agency, because a DAO can operate a governance structure built entirely on software, code, and smart contracts. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
