   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7663",
   "text": "Perspectives on digital innovation and the governance imperative: from E-business to AI-mediated decision systems presents the following source proposition: Each wave has not only altered how value is created but has also imposed new demands on the governance frameworks societies use to manage technological change. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The tension between the need for regulation and the desire for decentralization produces what the author terms the pacing problem: regulatory frameworks cannot keep pace with technological innovation, so the remedy lies in dynamic autonomous governance rather than static centralized control. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
