  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7628",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7628",
   "text": "Ethical AI and Corporate Governance: Exploring the Social Implications of AI-Driven Decision-Making in Business presents the following source proposition: While AI-driven systems offer significant benefits in terms of efficiency, accuracy, and predictive capabilities, they simultaneously raise critical ethical and governance concerns related to transparency, accountability, fairness, privacy, and stakeholder trust. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Even after recent reforms, the corporate governance framework remains framed in terms of hierarchy, which is why it fits poorly with looser and unmediated stakeholder relationships. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
