   "text": "Approaches and emerging trends in multi-agent autonomous AI systems for education innovation in Vietnam presents the following source proposition: Agentic artificial intelligence (AI) systems that act as autonomous agents are rapidly evolving due to the explosion of large language models (LLMs) [1]. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Regulation of legal AI faces a two sided failure: strict regimes such as the EU AI Act may stifle innovation, while lenient approaches such as the United States risk leaving biases unchecked. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
