   "text": "AI Governance in the United States: Using Game Theory to Promote Innovation and Uphold Ethical Standards By Yana Bijoor presents the following source proposition: The international AI landscape is complex, as countries act independently. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The decline in later stage robotics and drone investment rounds in the United States does not indicate stalled technological development; companies relocate later stage development to other countries because of the regulatory disconnect that exists in the United States. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
