   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7533",
   "text": "AI Governance in the United States: Using Game Theory to Promote Innovation and Uphold Ethical Standards By Yana Bijoor presents the following source proposition: Artificial Intelligence (AI) significantly impacts several industries by enhancing workplace productivity and influencing consumer decisions. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Regulation of legal AI faces a two sided failure: strict regimes such as the EU AI Act may stifle innovation, while lenient approaches such as the United States risk leaving biases unchecked. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
