   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7531",
   "text": "Chief Decision &amp;amp; Capital Officer (CDCO): A Governance-First Framework for Deterministic Decision Authority in AI-Driven Systems presents the following source proposition: However, despite these capabilities, modern systems lack a deterministic mechanism for validating decisions under uncertainty, irreversibility, and systemic risk. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Real world court decisions on smart contract disputes, even where attainable, may not carry the same legitimacy and authority for the parties as intra-blockchain dispute resolution mechanisms. The proposed response is a qualification: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
