  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7525",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7525",
   "text": "The Structural Selection of Nominal Human-in-the-Loop: Technical and Market Erosion Pressures in Accountability-Deficient AI Governance presents the following source proposition: In domains where AI has become the substantive decision-maker, human involvement is often maintained in form whilst the institutional means for externally verifying its substance are absent. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Accountability is a structural concern in DeFi: without a central entity it can become unclear who is responsible for wrongdoing, and when problems arise no central party can freeze transactions, fix problems, or restore normal operations. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
