   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7512",
   "text": "AI in Public Governance: Ensuring Rights and Innovation in Non-High-Risk AI Systems in the United States presents the following source proposition: This paper aims to contribute to the ongoing effort to create an AI governance framework that takes public confidence in AI policy into account. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Regulatory sandboxes are an instance of regulatory decentralization: by lowering regulatory barriers and costs for testing disruptive technologies while protecting consumers, the regulator fosters innovation in increasingly decentralized products and services. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
