   "text": "Streamlining Compliance and Governance with AI in Cloud-based Programs presents the following source proposition: Software as a Service (SaaS) is a prominent cloud computing model, providing potential cost-savings and improved cost control. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Waiver of rights provisions are the most prevalent governance term in the sample, appearing in 96 percent of agreements, followed by cooperation with the government at 91 percent and improved compliance programs at 75 percent. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
