   "text": "Streamlining Compliance and Governance with AI in Cloud-based Programs presents the following source proposition: Cloud-based programs offer numerous advantages to businesses and governments, including cost reduction, scalability, and on-demand services. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Existing corporate criminal liability combined with the absence of clear Department of Justice standards for charging businesses can push organizations to adopt unproven compliance programs and generate other inefficiencies. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
