   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7470",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7470",
   "text": "Algorithmic Governance and Responsible Innovation: AI Ethics Policy, Corporate Compliance, and Regulatory Quality in Chinese Technology Firms presents the following source proposition: Using a novel dataset of 187 publicly listed Chinese tech firms from 2019 to 2023, we use a difference-in-differences identification strategy that follows firm-level, staggered exposures to the provisions’ obligations. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that In companies that concentrate on established products, the executives who understand innovation and consumer experience, the very people responsible for the firm's initial success, are pushed to the margins of core decision making. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
