   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7469",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7469",
   "text": "Algorithmic Governance and Responsible Innovation: AI Ethics Policy, Corporate Compliance, and Regulatory Quality in Chinese Technology Firms presents the following source proposition: Algorithmic recommendation systems have become a foundational element of Chinese digital markets, managed by a string of firms under complex and often opaque governance regimes. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Many new innovation driven firms that replaced hierarchy with a best-idea-wins culture have struggled to maintain that governance model and to fulfill their initial promise. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
