  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7459",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7459",
   "text": "The AI Governance Market: Institutional Frameworks, Regulatory Architecture, and the Economics of Trust in Artificial Intelligence Systems presents the following source proposition: As AI systems increasingly influence critical decisions in healthcare, finance, public administration, and security, governance mechanisms have emerged as a central market and policy concern. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The literature offers high short term accuracy figures for judicial AI but almost no evidence on how these tools affect decision quality, case backlogs, or public trust over extended periods, which is a fundamental research gap. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
