   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7456",
   "text": "The artificial intelligence (AI) governance dilemma presents the following source proposition: The rapid diffusion of Artificial Intelligence (AI) across organizational and societal domains has exposed a tension between innovation, technological capability, and institutional responsibility. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Traditional hierarchical organizational structures are too slow to adapt to rapid technological change and stifle innovation through rigid control mechanisms, which is why they are unsuited to governing the quantum economy. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
