   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7454",
   "text": "Building Smarter Urban Ecosystems With IoT, AI, and Blockchain presents the following source proposition: Smart cities use emerging technologies such as the Internet of Things (IoT), artificial intelligence (AI), and blockchain to make urban environments more sustainable, efficient, and livable. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Critics who dismiss artificial intelligence on boards as science fiction not worth engaging are wrong: AI on boards is a real prospect, and technologies such as blockchain-based smart contracts will both disrupt corporate governance and supply solutions to it. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
