   "text": "Endogenous Observability and the Economics of Algorithmic Monitoring Applying and Extending the Hand Formula to AI Governance presents the following source proposition: This paper develops an economic analysis of algorithmic fairness monitoring requirements and does not constitute legal advice. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The published UDLC Codex deliberately left its DAO governance architecture unspecified because no existing decentralized governance paradigm could simultaneously satisfy the UDLC's requirements for real-time adaptivity, incorruptible expert meritocracy, jurisdictional neutrality, and long-term economic sustainability. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
