   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7449",
   "text": "The Uneven Inheritance: How 50 years of Telecom Policy Shape Today's AI Governance and Its Global Inequalities presents the following source proposition: Artificial intelligence is widely framed as a new regulatory frontier. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Privacy rules, copyright, and the uneven global distribution of digital connectivity independently reduce both the availability and the diversity of human-generated text for AI training. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
