   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7447",
   "text": "Bounded by Design: Applying the Donut Model to Responsible AI Implementation in Enterprise Operations A Practitioner Framework for AI Governance, Scale, and Accountability presents the following source proposition: Organizations deploy AI systems to drive efficiency, reduce headcount, and compress decision cycles-but rarely define the boundaries within which those systems should operate. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Accountability is a structural concern in DeFi: without a central entity it can become unclear who is responsible for wrongdoing, and when problems arise no central party can freeze transactions, fix problems, or restore normal operations. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
