   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7441",
   "text": "The Street Finds Its Own Uses for Attachment Human-Agent Relationships and the Hidden Economics of AI Collaboration presents the following source proposition: The economic analysis of AI agent usage focuses on token costs, API pricing, and compute efficiency. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Exponential improvement in compute efficiency combined with recursive self improvement of AI systems drives the marginal cost of additional intelligence and digital goods toward zero. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
