   "text": "Decoding Global AI Governance: A Computational Linguistic Analysis of National Regulations presents the following source proposition: Artificial Intelligence (AI) regulations addressing rights, usage limits, bias, and accountability mechanisms have been adopted by governments worldwide. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Solving data bias, computational overhead, stale datasets, privacy constraints, and inequitable compensation cannot be done within any single discipline; it requires concerted interdisciplinary effort across governments, corporations, researchers, and civil society. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
