   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7416",
   "text": "Corporate Involution in the Age of AI: The Governance and Cultural Drivers of Innovation presents the following source proposition: A one-standard-deviation increase in AI adoption raises the involution index by 10.5% of its standard deviation. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Many new innovation driven firms that replaced hierarchy with a best-idea-wins culture have struggled to maintain that governance model and to fulfill their initial promise. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
