   "text": "Experience Over Compliance: Why Frequent Use -Not Governance -Builds Managerial Trust in Generative AI presents the following source proposition: That question became the foundation of this doctoral research, which sought to bring empirical rigour to a gap the author encountered not in the literature, but in practice. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Form PF's counterparty disclosure proved far less burdensome in practice than anticipated: 93.75 percent of respondents encountered no difficulty identifying counterparties for the counterparty credit exposure questions. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
