   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7409",
   "text": "AI in Corporate Governance presents the following source proposition: Yet, alongside these efficiencies come profound challenges: algorithmic bias, opacity, and the erosion of human accountability. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that If a market evolves in which contingent capital designs appear to provide sufficient protection against systemic risk and contagion, decision makers may come to rely on the design of those securities and neglect their own role as monitors. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
