   "text": "Who Is Accountable? When AI Makes the Wrong Decision? Rethinking Corporate Governance presents the following source proposition: When one of these systems produces a harmful, discriminatory, or commercially damaging outcome, existing governance doctrine struggles to identify who answers for it. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The traditional fiduciary duty doctrine is one of the most amorphous concepts in the law, and its indeterminacy produces confusion, inconsistency, and cases with problematic outcomes. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
