   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7395",
   "text": "Bridging the governance and innovation gap in the generative AI market presents the following source proposition: The rapid diffusion of generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) systems, including large language and multimodal models, is increasingly outpacing existing policy and regulatory frameworks. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The rapid adoption of deep learning and predictive analytics in law was driven by two enabling conditions: the increasing availability of digitized legal data and the computational power to process it. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
