   "text": "The Compliance Evidence Gap: Why AI Governance Frameworks Stop Short at the Point of Proof presents the following source proposition: It is almost silent on how the truth of that demonstration is to be tested. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Weighted voting reduces Sybil attack success rates by over eighty-five percent, but only where reputation is openly auditable. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
