  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7382",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7382",
   "text": "Managing the Transparency and Trade Secret Conflict in AI Accountability: Layered Access as Governance Design presents the following source proposition: The dominant treatment of this conflict frames it as a doctrinal balancing exercise to be resolved through litigation or supervisory disclosure, as confirmed by the CJEU in Dun &amp;amp; Bradstreet. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Private foundations exercise plutocratic power because their leaders and trustees are not elected democratically, they are permitted to operate in perpetuity, and their operations lack accountability and transparency. The proposed response is a qualification: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
