   "text": "Managing the Transparency and Trade Secret Conflict in AI Accountability: Layered Access as Governance Design presents the following source proposition: Both interests are recognised under EU law and neither can be satisfied in full at the same time. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Neither weighted voting nor microsecond updates suffices alone; together they form a dual-layered defense because weighted voting addresses static identity proliferation while microsecond updates address dynamic behavioral exploitation. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
