   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7371",
   "text": "Governing AI-Generated Content: Labelling, Traceability and Transparency Infrastructure in China and the EU AI Act presents the following source proposition: It argues that AI-generated content labelling is neither a simple information-disclosure duty nor a purely technical detection problem. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Neither national nor international regulators have the resources to fully investigate or regulate hedge fund activity, and the industry actively lobbies to preserve the resulting information asymmetries. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
