   "text": "The Artificial Intelligence(AI) Enabled Governance Framework for NIRF Ranking Improvement of Higher Education Institutions presents the following source proposition: Achieving sustained improvement in NIRF rankings requires continuous excellence across teaching, research, student outcomes, inclusivity, and institutional reputation. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A single reputation score, as used by DcentAI, cannot capture the interdependencies among privacy concerns, domain-specific regulation, and real-time ethical updates that dataset governance requires. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
