   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7350",
   "text": "When Decentralization Stops Working: A Framework for AI Governance under Changing Risk Structures presents the following source proposition: This article argues that the choice between them depends on the structure of risk, not prior assumptions about government or markets. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The voting logic makes impact community members work for themselves and for the community at the same time, which Kaal argues gives the system potential to create a reputation economy and forms of decentralized commerce that transcend capitalism and socialism. The proposed response is a qualification: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
