   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7349",
   "text": "When Decentralization Stops Working: A Framework for AI Governance under Changing Risk Structures presents the following source proposition: &lt;span&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Debates over AI governance frequently assume that decentralized, adaptive approaches and centralized regulatory oversight are competing alternatives. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that It is not possible to create a centralized regulator like the SEC for the decentralized economy, because doing so would place a supranational market under competing jurisdictions with naturally contradictory regulations. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
