   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7345",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7345",
   "text": "Beyond Technical Compliance III: From Designed Fragilities to Cooperative AI-Whose Intentions, Whose Governance? presents the following source proposition: Current AI governance operates within a paradigm that treats system design as a technical challenge requiring technical solutions. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Although CIAs are not laws, they go beyond aspirational governance standards because they set forth concrete governance rules that more clearly define the duties to be informed, to exercise oversight, and to maintain effective reporting systems, thereby requiring a higher standard of care. The proposed response is a qualification: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
