   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7340",
   "text": "Monitoring AI progress for corporate governance presents the following source proposition: While AI is believed to increase both the productivity and competitive advantage, it will lead to rapid transformation in the work force and evolve with a high degree of uncertainty. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Companies that adopt unmediated and technology-driven governance gain a competitive advantage in attracting talent, raising capital, finding partners, and above all in remaining relevant in hyper-competitive global markets. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
