   "text": "Closing the AI Proof Gap: An Evidence Architecture for Operationalizing NIST AI RMF, ISO/IEC 42001, and EU AI Act Requirements Across Board Governance, Regulatory Disclosure, and D&amp;amp;O Underwriting presents the following source proposition: First, it defines the AI Proof Gap as an analytic category distinct from, but related to, prior work on AI accountability, algorithmic auditing, and ethics washing. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Prior scholarship, including the author's own earlier work, established that Form PF created core challenges for the private fund industry but did not clarify what impact the disclosure requirements actually have on managers; this study is designed to fill that gap. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
