   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7306",
   "text": "Multi-agent Interaction presents the following source proposition: With the development of AI agents, there is an opportunity to enable agents to discuss with each other using natural language. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The real barrier to multi agent competition is not cost but the absence of an attribution mechanism: if only the best of several competing agents is paid, the others have no incentive to participate, so competition requires rewards proportional to each contributor's contribution. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
