   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7293",
   "text": "Can AI governance be progressive? Group interests, group privacy and abnormal justice presents the following source proposition: This paper asks whether our current thin concept of responsibility can be made into a thicker one that takes in more than compliance with law and basic ethical principles. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Smart contracts can automate compliance with regulatory requirements and ethical guidelines: for example, a smart contract can enforce privacy law directly by controlling an AI system's access to personal data according to predefined rules. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
