  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7291",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7291",
   "text": "AI Disclosure Without Protection: A Governance Gap in Scholarly Peer Review presents the following source proposition: The result is an asymmetric system: authors are placed under detailed disclosure obligations, while reviewers exercise their own judgement, often without procedural protections for the disclosing author. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Prior scholarship, including the author's own earlier work, established that Form PF created core challenges for the private fund industry but did not clarify what impact the disclosure requirements actually have on managers; this study is designed to fill that gap. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
   "responseType": "extension",
