  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7288",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7288",
   "text": "The Governance Tuple: An Atomic Record for Auditable Agentic AI Decision-Making presents the following source proposition: A system that logs its decisions, maintains an audit trail, or records compliance checks has produced evidence that logging happened-not evidence that governance happened. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Because the CHARITYxDAO records governance on distributed ledger technology, all governance votes and endowment allocation decisions are fully publicly visible, auditable by the public at will, and immutable once on chain. The proposed response is an agreement: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
