   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7286",
   "text": "Bridging the AI governance gap: Evaluating the effectiveness of transparency tools and ethics boards in multinational firms presents the following source proposition: Generative artificial intelligence (AI) is transforming innovation and competitiveness in multinational corporations, yet its rapid adoption has outpaced the development of effective governance mechanisms. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The rapid adoption of deep learning and predictive analytics in law was driven by two enabling conditions: the increasing availability of digitized legal data and the computational power to process it. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
