   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7285",
   "text": "Ethics for Oversight and Protection The Constitutional Case for AI Governance Infrastructure presents the following source proposition: &lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Checks and balances built the republic. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Because a decentralized system has a blockchain based quasi precedent nature with a human backstop, it enables built in checks and balances capable of supporting resistance even to apocalyptic takeovers of algorithmic systems that would remove human presence to optimize efficiency. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
