   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7282",
   "text": "&lt;p&gt;The Governance Gap in AI Arbitration&lt;/p&gt; presents the following source proposition: The release of America's AI Action Plan in 2025 provides an essential lens for understanding this transformation. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Reputation functions as a social incentive that complements monetary reward and sustains cooperation in trustless environments, a behavioral mechanism unavailable to purely stake-weighted consensus systems. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
