   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7275",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7275",
   "text": "AICOS: A Governance-First Deterministic Decision Infrastructure for Human-Final AI Systems presents the following source proposition: However, they remain fundamentally limited in decision authority, governance, and auditability. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The code is law paradigm departs from existing legal systems in three linked ways: it shifts authority from sovereign institutions to technical protocols, replaces interpretive flexibility with deterministic enforcement, and substitutes technological neutrality for normative deliberation. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
