   "mappingConfidence": 0.3749,
   "mappingAmbiguous": true
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7270",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7270",
   "text": "Experimentalism beyond ex ante regulation: A law and economics perspective on AI regulatory sandboxes presents the following source proposition: In response, experimentalist governance–particularly through regulatory sandboxes (RSs)–has emerged as a potential solution. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Governance adjustments made through stable rules in reaction to a systemic shock can result in suboptimal governance outcomes, market volatility, and economic loss. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
