   "mappingConfidence": 0.3595,
   "mappingAmbiguous": true
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7267",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7267",
   "text": "Blockchain and AI: The technological revolution’s impact on corporate governance relationships presents the following source proposition: Through the creation of decentralized and more efficient systems able to process information at a higher speed than any human, Blockchain and artificial intelligence are the answer to these renewal requests. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Despite the obvious benefits of technology applications in corporate governance, the technological revolution has not yet produced wide acceptance of unmediated or decentralized corporate governance structures and practices. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
