  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7263",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7263",
   "text": "Building Trustworthy AI: Transparency, Fairness, and Governance in the Digital Age presents the following source proposition: Our analysis reveals that achieving trustworthy AI requires not merely technical solutions but a comprehensive approach that combines technological innovation with robust social governance mechanisms. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that In early Silicon Valley the contractual mechanisms lawyers designed, together with the lawyer dominated market for reputation, reduced information asymmetries between entrepreneurs and investors and were necessary to bring the demand and supply sides of venture capital together effectively. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
