   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7260",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7260",
   "text": "AI-Augmented Corporate Governance: Enhancing the Effectiveness of Independent Directors presents the following source proposition: However, increasing organizational complexity, information asymmetry between boards and management, and the growing volume of regulatory and operational data have significantly constrained the ability of Independent Directors to discharge their fiduciary duties effectively. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Courts assume that the boards of companies that executed a CIA have more knowledge and can exercise more control, and therefore hold those directors to a heightened fiduciary duty, rejecting directors' claims of ignorance because executing a CIA or a CIA like agreement means directors do know or should know about the noncompliance. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-07-31",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
