   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7253",
   "text": "Understanding Decoupling in Bank Corporate Governance Through a Critical Review of Corporate Governance Theories presents the following source proposition: A critical review is provided on three main CG perspectives: shareholder, stakeholder and institutional. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Allowing minorities onto the board increases creativity through the different perspectives they represent, which acts as a defense against groupthink. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
