   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7252",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7252",
   "text": "Measuring Governance Architecture: Adaptive AI Oversight and the Innovation-Penalty Debate presents the following source proposition: Comparative AI governance research typically codes countries as treated upon strategy adoption or regulation. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Financial innovation, the globalization of markets, transnationalism, ethical challenges, and the bounded rationality of humans are likely to create and increase future challenges that require additional and more extensive governance adjustments. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
