   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7250",
   "text": "AI and Structural Injustice presents the following source proposition: Structural injustice has an analytical and evaluative component. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The standard welfare theorems lose their foundation in the computative domain, and while human welfare plausibly remains the evaluative criterion at the terminal level, the apparatus connecting intermediate agent-to-agent activity to terminal human welfare remains undeveloped. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
