   "text": "Margin and Cost Optimization Governance for Cloud and AI Businesses presents the following source proposition: &lt;p&gt;As cloud, AI, and agentic systems reshape business economics, margin outcomes are increasingly influenced by usage behavior, cost-to-serve dynamics, and pricing decisions that evolve at different speeds. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Humans remain the terminal consumers of AI generated value but cease to be its proximate driver, and this distinction is why traditional demand side economics loses descriptive accuracy in the agentic layer. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
