   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7236",
   "text": "Technocratic Capture: Reflexive Values and the Governance of AI Harm presents the following source proposition: When fairness becomes a metric, accountability an audit, and transparency a disclosure form, something happens to the values themselves. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Weighted voting works as a Sybil defense only under two conditions: reputation metrics must capture meaningful effort such as block production quality and depth of governance participation, and the system must maintain continuous transparency backed by community oversight and formal verification. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
