  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7203",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7203",
   "text": "Beyond the AI race: why global governance is the greatest innovation presents the following source proposition: As artificial intelligence (AI) evolves rapidly, the urgency to govern it responsibly becomes more pressing by the day. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Critics who dismiss artificial intelligence on boards as science fiction not worth engaging are wrong: AI on boards is a real prospect, and technologies such as blockchain-based smart contracts will both disrupt corporate governance and supply solutions to it. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
