   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7202",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7202",
   "text": "From Responsibility to Safety: AI Governance in the EU's General-Purpose AI Code of Practice presents the following source proposition: As part of the AI Act implementation, the European Commission has introduced the GeneralPurpose AI Code of Practice (the “Code”), a supplement to the Act meant to outline how compliance can be achieved for providers of “general-purpose” AI models. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Generic industry advice on building an effective compliance program cannot work in practice because it is written to apply to many firms at once while no two companies are sufficiently alike for general guidance to be effective. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
