   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7199",
   "text": "Defining organizational AI governance presents the following source proposition: However, there have been few efforts to define AI governance thus far. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Put option based discount models for lack of marketability have been widely used, but they can be inaccurate because real investors do not possess perfect market timing ability. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
