   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7196",
   "text": "AI Governance as a Strategic Marketing Capability presents the following source proposition: Artificial intelligence has transformed how organizations collect, interpret, and act upon customer information. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Well-capitalized centralized incumbents can outpace decentralized entrants in user acquisition by leveraging existing customer bases and brand recognition, so decentralized startups must show clear advantages in compensation, transparency, or data protection to win adoption. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
