   "text": "AI-Powered Corporate Governance presents the following source proposition: These firms also undertake fewer but higher-quality acquisitions and produce fewer but more valuable patents, indicating improved investment efficiency in real decisions. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The extent to which a company uses data and algorithms will separate the winning companies of the future from the rest, because algorithmically driven firms gather consumer behavior data and instantaneously feed it back into an improved consumer experience. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
