   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7191",
   "text": "The Economics of Agentic AI: Runtime Governance as a Distinct Determinant of Enterprise AI Cost presents the following source proposition: Runtime semantic authorization adds a distinct control question: whether an exposed Operational Interpretation carries institutional authority to proceed. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Institutional investors face a distinct barrier beyond volatility: fiduciary responsibility to their clients limits the type of risk they may take on, and the lack of custody solutions recognized by regulators compounds the problem. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
