   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7189",
   "text": "The Economics of Agentic AI: Runtime Governance as a Distinct Determinant of Enterprise AI Cost presents the following source proposition: Per-token inference prices are falling, while agentic workflows increase the number of model interactions, tool calls, and downstream actions required to complete a task. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Under a deflationary token issuance model, which caps the number of tokens ever issued, prices are expected to increase because of the fundamental scarcity of token supply. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
