   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7179",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7179",
   "text": "MEG1 (Minimal Ethical Governance v5.0): A Technical Standard for Verifiable AI Governance presents the following source proposition: &lt;div&gt; Artificial intelligence governance frameworks commonly define principles such as accountability, transparency, safety, fairness, and human oversight, but often lack a unified technical layer through which compliance can be continuously measured, independently verified, and transferred across systems, operators, and jurisdictions. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Decentralized data production will succeed only if it solves fraudulent submissions, content moderation, and alignment with ethical and legal frameworks; these are necessary conditions, not incidental risks. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
