   "text": "AI Governance and Geopolitics presents the following source proposition: This paper offers a three-level analytical framework for AI geopolitics. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Demand-side analyses that assume a proximate-consumption structure lose descriptive accuracy where the computative primitive holds, because most transactions occur among agents; welfare analysis in those domains must therefore be conducted at the terminal rather than the proximate level. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
