  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7158",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7158",
   "text": "Understanding agent governance technology approaches presents the following source proposition: Agent artificial intelligence (AI) automates AI using the reasoning power of large language models (LLMs) to make decisions without human intervention. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The Shenzhen courts illustrate a workable three step human-in-the-loop design for generative judicial AI: the judge decides first, the LLM generates the supporting reasoning, and the judge then revises that output to finalize the judgment. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
