   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7146",
   "text": "Key Technologies of a Service Platform Based on Blockchain Technology presents the following source proposition: Blockchain has the characteristics of decentralization, stability, security, and tamper-proof. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Platform centralization is especially damaging in developer communities because developers are the channel through which information from the edges of the system and society enters, and through which consensus on emerging technologies is formed. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
