  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7070",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7070",
   "text": "Shaping Decentralized Collaboration in DAOs with a Requirements Engineering Framework presents the following source proposition: Distributed Autonomous Organizations (DAOs) introduce novel governance and collaboration challenges by decentralizing decision-making and automating organizational processes via blockchain smart contracts. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A decentralized autonomous organization is merely computer code with no directors, managers or employees, its governance structure built with software, code and smart contracts running on a public decentralized blockchain platform. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
