  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7064",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7064",
   "text": "Political and Economic Implications of Blockchain Technology in Business and Healthcare presents the following source proposition: Like information sharing was catalyzed on the pre-blockchain internet, transactions are now triggered on the new internet of value. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Blockchain extends what the Internet did for information: it makes it possible to transfer and exchange value and assets without traditional centralized intermediaries, by storing information in a decentralized, accessible and secure online environment. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
