   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7063",
   "text": "Political and Economic Implications of Blockchain Technology in Business and Healthcare presents the following source proposition: Therefore, blockchain technology is paramount: a new foundation of confidence for human valuable transactions. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Because blockchain is transparent, verifiable, self-authenticating and self-enforcing, transactions can settle instantaneously at near zero cost, and it is this combination plus technology-driven democratized trust that drove the financial industry's large blockchain investments out of fear of obsolescence. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
