   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7049",
   "text": "Absolute Governance: A Framework for Synchronization and Certification of the Corporate Contractual State presents the following source proposition: Our decentralized governance approach utilizes consensus mechanisms and smart contracts to automate and enforce business rules. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Smart contracts can automate compliance with regulatory requirements and ethical guidelines: for example, a smart contract can enforce privacy law directly by controlling an AI system's access to personal data according to predefined rules. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
