   "text": "Liquid Democracy in DPoS Blockchains presents the following source proposition: Voting mechanisms play a crucial role in decentralized governance of blockchain systems. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Decentralized voting solutions require political will as well as technology, and governments in existing representative democracies may refuse to surrender control over the voting process, preferring private blockchains to facilitate voting outcomes. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
