   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7043",
   "text": "Hackchain: A Blockchain-Based Framework for Fair and Transparent Hackathons presents the following source proposition: Hackathons are collaborative events where individuals with diverse backgrounds come together to develop innovative projects within a short timeframe. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The WDAG system preserves legal history as a byproduct of its architecture: all legal precedents are retained within a blockchain based framework in a transparent and immutable format, so historical access does not trade off against current relevance. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
