   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7039",
   "text": "A Blockchain Token Economy Model for Financing a Decentralized Electric Vehicle Charging Platform presents the following source proposition: Recent advances in distributed ledger technologies enable new types of decentralized governance and financing for technology platforms. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Recentralization is the central obstacle to using blockchain and distributed ledger technology to govern AI: the recentralizing tendency of these networks interferes with their capacity to deliver effective AI governance. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
