   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7038",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7038",
   "text": "Decentralized Platforms: Governance, Tokenomics, and ICO Design presents the following source proposition: Although commission contracts often lead to higher profits for founders, token retention leads to higher service levels, benefiting the users and service providers. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Even after the ICO boom of 2017 and 2018, many digital asset projects and token launches are designed with the primary focus on benefiting the founding group, which often finds creative ways to cash out of the project after a successful run. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
