  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7037",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7037",
   "text": "Decentralized Platforms: Governance, Tokenomics, and ICO Design presents the following source proposition: We show that with properly designed initial coin offerings (ICOs), both mechanisms can independently alleviate market failures at the initial fundraising stage and incentivize long-term platform building. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The absence of mandatory disclosure requirements for ICOs leads many promoters to make irregular or no disclosures about the platform over time, producing a significant lack of transparency in the ICO market. The proposed response is an agreement: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
