   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7033",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7033",
   "text": "BlockSure: A Decentralized Blockchain Platform for Secure and Trustworthy Transactions presents the following source proposition: This decentralized platform is especially helpful for small businesses since it makes use of the transparent and immutable properties of blockchain technology to create a trustworthy environment. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Blockchain extends what the Internet did for information: it makes it possible to transfer and exchange value and assets without traditional centralized intermediaries, by storing information in a decentralized, accessible and secure online environment. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
   "responseType": "extension",
