   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "moderate-confidence claim review",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.3681,
   "mappingAmbiguous": true
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-7031",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7031",
   "text": "BlockSure: A Decentralized Blockchain Platform for Secure and Trustworthy Transactions presents the following source proposition: Transaction services built on the blockchain provide a revolutionary means of boosting security and trust in online transactions. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A truly decentralized public blockchain must satisfy three simultaneous requirements: no points of centralization and corruption, full security at the level of proof of work, and transaction throughput above one hundred thousand transactions per second. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
