   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-7019",
   "text": "Blockchain Technology, Challenges and Opportunities presents the following source proposition: It allows both participatory and decentralized governance, but is also the expression of unbridled liberalism, the enemy of democracy. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that AI powered DAOs that autonomously generate revenue are especially hard to regulate or dismantle, because the same blockchain security features that protect the organization also make it difficult to intervene once it is operational. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
