   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6989",
   "text": "Blockchain-enabled Carbon Dioxide Removal: A Decentralized Framework for Transparent and Scalable Climate Mitigation presents the following source proposition: Key innovations include a dynamic consensus mechanism for real-time stakeholder collaboration and cryptographic protocols for secure, auditable record-keeping. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The core issues that afflict centralized governance solutions, including information asymmetries, censorship, opportunism of agents, breaches of fiduciary duties, and fraud, can only be truly removed if and when a truly decentralized public blockchain emerges that is scalable and fully secure. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
