   "text": "Blockchain Access Control Based on Continuous Trust Evaluation presents the following source proposition: Data privacy protection has thus emerged as a critically important topic. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Although blockchain technology itself offers unprecedented data and privacy protection, storing blockchain data across a global network of nodes often will not comply with the consumer protection rules, directives, and guidelines of particular jurisdictions. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
