   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6966",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6966",
   "text": "The end of labor economics as we know it: DSGM and the shift to a 3D economy- a case study of Denmark’s transformation into a talent stock market presents the following source proposition: The traditional labor market, constrained by time and place, is increasingly inadequate for the demands of the digital age. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Because the new solutions rewarded by the future labor market will be code based, an understanding of code and coding will be essential to participate effectively in the digital world. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
