   "text": "Performance analysis on Diversity Mining‐based Proof of Work in bifolded consortium blockchain for Internet of Things consensus presents the following source proposition: But, the prevailing centralized IoT architecture has numerous security vulnerabilities, specifically in data hosting and transfer. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Existing blockchains and DAOs still lack genuine decentralization, and there are currently no true DAOs: Bitcoin's proof of work protocol has produced mining pools because of economies of scale and unbalanced reward structures. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
