   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6963",
   "text": "Performance analysis on Diversity Mining‐based Proof of Work in bifolded consortium blockchain for Internet of Things consensus presents the following source proposition: In the present‐day scenario, IoT networks are distributed, and they generate heterogeneous data to be shared, processed and analyzed. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The data mining that produces scarcity in existing blockchains also slows creation, so high speed transactions cannot be achieved for the foreseeable future without a different consensus design. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
