   "text": "Decentralized finance as a Web 3.0 information system: a state-of-the-art survey presents the following source proposition: It synthesizes how DeFi mechanisms are structured across architectural, functional and governance dimensions and clarifies how they reshape trust, coordination, transparency and accountability in decentralized digital environments. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Becoming an OCC regulated trust is one route by which crypto exchanges can operate nationwide without securing state level licenses in each of the 49 states that require one. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
