   "text": "Ecosystem Implementations in Smart City through Blockchain Technology presents the following source proposition: Smart cities are structured on smart devices to govern urban management. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Smart contracting on a blockchain often makes conventional legal contracting unnecessary, because smart contracts emulate the logic of legal contract clauses. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
