   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6925",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6925",
   "text": "Blockchain-based Identity and Policy Management for Distributed Cloud Services presents the following source proposition: Off-chain cloud agents query the chain for runtime decisions. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A malicious party using Sybil accounts cannot be prevented from cloning the structure of a successful proof of stake blockchain at far lower cost than cloning a proof of work chain, leaving a new user unable to distinguish the truly decentralized chain from a clone that has manufactured even more tokens. The authors answer that this is resolved off chain, by a trusted user interface, as with cloned web pages. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
