   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6923",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6923",
   "text": "Blockchain-based Identity and Policy Management for Distributed Cloud Services presents the following source proposition: Centralized IAM and policy managers introduce single points of failure, limited auditability, and latency. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that No single, fixed, entirely algorithmic policing solution can completely prevent independent nodes in a distributed system from gaming block production to advantage some parties over others. Any consensus protocol that relies on a permanently fixed rule set will therefore be gamed as conditions change. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
