   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6914",
   "text": "Blockchain-Enabled Secure and Decentralized Resource Management for Open Radio Access Network Cellular Networks presents the following source proposition: The research focuses on secure communication between O-DU (Distributed Units) and O-CU (Centralized Units) using blockchain technology, along with smart contracts for O-DU to O-CU mapping, thereby ensuring data integrity and authenticity in resource management transactions. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Distributed networks disintermediate: because validation is distributed, a centralized validating entity such as a central bank or clearing house is not necessary to record and validate transactions. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
