   "text": "The <scp>Unidroit</scp> Principles and the inflexibility of code as law: reconciling smart contracts with general clauses presents the following source proposition: These technologies follow a deterministic, if/then logic that is often difficult to reconcile with the inherent malleability of contract law. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Smart contracts fail to accommodate human business interaction because code does not follow the same logic on similar terms as natural human language, so the flexibility in interpreting intent that human dealings require cannot be ensured. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
