   "text": "Potential Applications of Blockchain and Crypto-Assets in Construction Industry & Management:- A Review presents the following source proposition: Blockchain technol-ogy (BCT) & Crypto Currencies (CC) promises to ensure that data is secure, decentralized, and immutable. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Supervisory tasks traditionally performed by principals to control their agents can be delegated to decentralized computer networks that are reliable, secure, immutable, and independent of fallible human input and discretionary human goodwill. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
