   "text": "Blockchain and Tokenization of Good Governance presents the following source proposition: Blockchain’s promise is to reduce agency costs and increase connectivity across markets. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Cryptographic hashes increase blockchain security and remove the trust barriers in agency relationships that otherwise require monitoring of agents and generate agency costs. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
