   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6651",
   "text": "Delving into the Security Side of Decentralized Finance Applications presents the following source proposition: Moreover, we propose a classification framework for existing various DeFi DApps. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The legacy private investment fund model delays liquidity: the investment process is long, complex and time intensive and leads up to a very late liquidity event in the form of an IPO or acquisition, which is why funds seek the early liquidity cryptocurrencies provide. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
