   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6647",
   "text": "Concentration in Governance Control Across Decentralised Finance Protocols presents the following source proposition: Blockchain-based systems are frequently governed through tokens that grant their holders voting rights over core protocol functions and funds. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that In a decentralized autonomous organization a series of smart contracts grants token holders voting rights, so the blockchain-based smart contract performs the function that articles of incorporation or bylaws perform in a conventional company. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
