   "text": "Enhancing Corporate Governance with Blockchain and Smart Contracts: A Systematic Review of Agency Conflict Mitigation presents the following source proposition: We followed PRISMA reporting guidance and searched Scopus for English journal articles published between 2018 and 2025. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A blockchain guarantee means that a contract between principal and agent executes only if and when all contract parameters have been fulfilled by both parties and verified by a majority of miners or nodes in the system. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
