   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6605",
   "text": "Effective Targeted Testing of Smart Contracts presents the following source proposition: Since smart contracts are immutable, their bugs cannot be fixed, which may lead to significant monetary losses. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Losses from smart contract vulnerabilities are large and growing, with 2021 losses alone estimated at 680 million dollars and cumulative global losses estimated at over 6 billion dollars. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
