   "text": "Refinement of estimates of the success probability of a double-spend attack on the Blockchain System, Based on the Independent Players Model presents the following source proposition: The transparency of blockchain systems makes it possible to store publicly available and irrefutable records. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that No single, fixed, entirely algorithmic policing solution can completely prevent independent nodes in a distributed system from gaming block production to advantage some parties over others. Any consensus protocol that relies on a permanently fixed rule set will therefore be gamed as conditions change. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
