   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6583",
   "text": "Digital Jurisdiction: Model presents the following source proposition: Digital jurisdiction is interpreted as a tool for civilizational adaptation of law to the age of Web 4.0, blockchain legal protocols and artificial intelligence. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Real world court decisions on smart contract disputes, even where attainable, may not carry the same legitimacy and authority for the parties as intra-blockchain dispute resolution mechanisms. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
