   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6581",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6581",
   "text": "Design and Implementation of a Blockchain-Enabled Crowdfunding Platform for Secure Transactions presents the following source proposition: Blockchain technology provides a decentralized and secure way to conduct financial transactions without intermediaries. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Business, administrative, and legal processes that depend on legal intermediaries may become redundant as blockchain technology advances and is accepted, with ledger keeping services such as notary and registry services, motions practice, and title companies among the first to disappear. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
