  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6576",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6576",
   "text": "A Deep Analysis of Blockchain Technology from Socio-Economic and Technological Perspectives: Intrinsic Barriers and Potential Impact presents the following source proposition: We (i) characterize cryptocurrency as one-tiered collateralized money. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The interoperability deficit in cryptocurrency markets is partly intrinsic to blockchain technology itself, because the consensus mechanism that allows block propagation on one chain in some ways negates interoperability with other chains and their consensus. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
