   "text": "Consortium blockchain for an intelligent transport system presents the following source proposition: The proposed messages are intended to be exchanged not only between vehicles and road infrastructure but between vehicles as well. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Contemporary blockchains cannot support the proposed architecture because the technology is too slow and expensive to poll members on every transaction, and the messages required for all nodes to register all votes on every action multiply into an unmanageable number. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
