   "text": "Innovation and Evolution of Business Models in the Lazy Economy under the Platform Economy presents the following source proposition: The rapid rise of the platform economy and the “lazy economy” is driven by the proliferation of the internet and the fast pace of modern life. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Internet based platform businesses and distributed ledger technology businesses have not reached their full potential, and the core factor holding them back is worldwide decreasing trust in the internet together with under developed trust in decentralized technology solutions. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
