   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6511",
   "text": "SoK: Blockchain-Based Decentralized AI (DeAI) presents the following source proposition: To address these issues, blockchain-based Decentralized Artificial Intelligence (DeAI) has emerged as a promising paradigm that leverages decentralization and transparency to improve the trustworthiness of AI systems. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Private fund advisers' increasing use of blockchain technology, artificial intelligence, and big data is a distinct source of downward pressure on the traditional 2/20 fee structure that commentators have not examined. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
