   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6509",
   "text": "Study and Design of Blockchain Based Decentralized Trust Management System for Secure Transactions presents the following source proposition: However, the complex issue of transaction security remains difficult to address. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A truly decentralized public blockchain must satisfy three simultaneous requirements: no points of centralization and corruption, full security at the level of proof of work, and transaction throughput above one hundred thousand transactions per second. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
