   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6492",
   "text": "Cryptocurrency and the SEC: How a Piecemeal Approach to Regulating New Technology Selectively Stifles Innovation presents the following source proposition: While some cryptocurrencies, like those involved in capital-raising via initial coin offerings (ICOs), do indeed seem like securities, others do not. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Initial coin offerings have overtaken venture capital as a funding channel for blockchain start ups, raising 331 million dollars in twelve months, and may become an alternative funding method for traditional companies as well. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
