   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6468",
   "text": "Smart Contracts: Tales of Trust and Certainty presents the following source proposition: Contrary to the popular narrative, smart contracts do not eliminate the need for trust and are technically incapable of guaranteeing performance. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The hope of most Web3 engineers that overhead institutions can be automated away until they vanish is largely misplaced, because business contracts are not getting simpler as technology becomes more sophisticated. The proposed response is a contradiction: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
