   "text": "A Blockchain-Driven Cyber-Systemic Approach to Hybrid Reality presents the following source proposition: Hybrid Reality (HyR) is the place where human beings and artificial entities interact. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Legacy systems at private investment funds and banks are more expensive, more error prone, and slower than emerging blockchain technologies, a gap illustrated by the $1.7 trillion in processing fees banks charged in 2014. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
