   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6398",
   "text": "AI and Blockchain: Transforming Digital Transactions presents the following source proposition: The synergy between AI and Blockchain is the focus of this study, which also looks at how their integration has a profound effect on transaction security, efficiency, and transparency. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Because blockchain is transparent, verifiable, self-authenticating and self-enforcing, transactions can settle instantaneously at near zero cost, and it is this combination plus technology-driven democratized trust that drove the financial industry's large blockchain investments out of fear of obsolescence. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
