   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6397",
   "text": "AI and Blockchain: Transforming Digital Transactions presents the following source proposition: Blockchain technology and Artificial Intelligence (AI) can potentially change the way digital transactions are conducted. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Private fund advisers' increasing use of blockchain technology, artificial intelligence, and big data is a distinct source of downward pressure on the traditional 2/20 fee structure that commentators have not examined. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
