   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6396",
   "text": "AI and Blockchain: Transforming Digital Transactions presents the following source proposition: In the digital age of today, keeping transactions safe and effective has become increasingly important. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Because blockchain network nodes verify, validate and audit transactions both before and after execution, the model is safer than a traditional one in which transactions can only be accomplished through third party intermediaries such as a bank, judiciary or notary. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
