   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6394",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6394",
   "text": "Are Cryptocurrency Forks Wealth Creating? presents the following source proposition: Involuntary forks that are forced due to hacks and other problems with the blockchain are not. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The interoperability deficit in cryptocurrency markets is partly intrinsic to blockchain technology itself, because the consensus mechanism that allows block propagation on one chain in some ways negates interoperability with other chains and their consensus. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
