  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6227",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6227",
   "text": "Cryptogatekeepers as a Response to Conflicts in Decentralized Finance presents the following source proposition: Cryptoenterprises—known as financial Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs)—operate without traditional corporate governance mechanisms such as boards of directors or managerial oversight, which only rely on computer code for governance. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A decentralized autonomous organization is merely computer code with no directors, managers or employees, its governance structure built with software, code and smart contracts running on a public decentralized blockchain platform. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
