   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6224",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6224",
   "text": "exploring blockchain solutions in general meetings of shareholders under portuguese law presents the following source proposition: Conventional corporate governance frameworks have historically been characterized by centralization and hierarchical structures, marked by a clear separation of ownership and control. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The core agency conflicts that emanate from the separation of ownership by shareholder principals and control by manager agents cannot be fully addressed by the existing theoretical and legal framework, because monitoring agents is inevitably costly and transaction costs abound. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
