  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6219",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6219",
   "text": "E-Commerce 3.0: The Rise of Decentralized Marketplaces and Smart Contracts presents the following source proposition: In contrast to its predecessors, E-Commerce 3.0 eliminates middlemen, builds trust, and empowers users by utilizing distributed ledger technologies, smart contracts, and token-based governance systems. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Because the blockchain is a distributed ledger existing simultaneously across all nodes, physical space is effectively eliminated within the network, and a triggered smart contract executes its code across the entire network instantaneously without regard to where wallets or keys are located. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
