   "text": "The Legal Meaning of Smart Contracts presents the following source proposition: Résume: Le présent article étudie la dimension juridique de contrats intelligents. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Smart contracting on the blockchain often makes legal contracting unnecessary because smart contracts emulate the logic of legal contract clauses. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
