  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6215",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6215",
   "text": "Advanced Topics for Blockchain‐Based Applications presents the following source proposition: As blockchain technology matures, the pursuit of innovative applications encounters a spectrum of complexities that extend beyond the foundational principles. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Traditional jurisdictional principles cannot directly apply to blockchain technology because the blockchain is merely a collection of agreed upon calculations by decentralized computer systems, and no particular node holds the entire blockchain. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
