  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6213",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6213",
   "text": "Loan Portfolio Dataset From MakerDAO Blockchain Project presents the following source proposition: Decentralized finance (DeFi) offers a range of financial instruments and services that leverage the capabilities of web3 technology. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Decentralized finance is structurally disadvantaged against traditional finance because decentralized products must be backed with full collateral, typically 100 percent and 200 percent on secondary layers such as MakerDAO, a collateralization burden that would be unthinkable in traditional markets. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
