  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6211",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6211",
   "text": "Civil law issues of Smart Contracts: Focusing on the DAO case presents the following source proposition: 한편 최근에는 이더리움(Ethereum) 등 블록체인 위에서 구현되는 DApps(Decentralized Applications)를 의미하는 용어로도 사용된다. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A decentralized autonomous organization is merely computer code with no directors, managers or employees, its governance structure built with software, code and smart contracts running on a public decentralized blockchain platform. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
