   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6201",
   "text": "Promoting Transparent and Scalable Decision-Making with IS Governance Framework: An Blockchain Approach presents the following source proposition: Objective: The study aims to design and assess an IS governance framework that allows to improve transparency, participation, and scalability in governance-related aspects of digital platforms, based on blockchain technology. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that DAO accountability comes from the recording mechanism itself: because all transactions and decisions are written to an immutable blockchain that every stakeholder can inspect, no single actor can easily manipulate or obscure organizational activity. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
