   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6146",
   "text": "Blockchain‐powered DeFi presents the following source proposition: Traditional models of water infrastructure investment finance have been marred by numerous obstacles that limit their efficiency, coverage and scalability. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Private fund advisers' increasing use of blockchain technology, artificial intelligence, and big data is a distinct source of downward pressure on the traditional 2/20 fee structure that commentators have not examined. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
