   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6145",
   "text": "Enacting Accountability in Decentralized Organizations: A Study of the Optimism Collective DAO presents the following source proposition: In centralized organizations, hierarchical structures clearly define accountability. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Absent continual effort to maintain decentralized order, the very values that initially unite DAO members tend to produce ever tighter and more complex hierarchical structures inside the DAO, ending in a fully centralized tree structure. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
