   "text": "What Is Money and a Brief History of It? presents the following source proposition: The chapter connects these concepts directly to smart contract development by examining real-world applications ranging from tokenized real estate to decentralized autonomous organizations (DAOs). This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A jurisdiction is only truly favorable to DAOs if it grants the DAO limited liability as an entity and accepts its independent status without requiring any representative in that jurisdiction. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
