   "text": "DAOs and Corporate Governance presents the following source proposition: DAOs challenge traditional conventions about corporate governance in several ways. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that On-chain governance systems outperform traditional governance models in responsiveness only if they incorporate robust anti-collusion measures, a requirement SPoS meets through its cryptographic commitments. The proposed response is a qualification: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
