   "text": "AI-driven DAOs presents the following source proposition: This algorithmic governance model proposes combining the decentralized and deterministic nature of DAOs with the autonomous and adaptable capabilities of AI agents. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that There is no consistent standard for DAO governance, which pushes each DAO to invent its own structure, and because decentralized governance is complex many of those structures fail to become truly decentralized, autonomous, or organized. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
