   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6099",
   "text": "DAOs Are Adaptive Governance Engines presents the following source proposition: DAOs, which are a species of firm made of smart contracts, seem to extend this logic. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Inexpensive open source smart contracts eliminate a major motivation for creating a firm under Coase's transaction cost theory, because they enable trustworthy transactions of any size with minimal transaction cost and high transaction security. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
