   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6094",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6094",
   "text": "Data Sheet 4_Not just code: a framework for community governance and management in Decentralized Autonomous Organizations.csv presents the following source proposition: The concept of Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs) has introduced a novel paradigm in organizational governance, characterized by more collaborative decision-making. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The decentralized power structure is supposed to encourage cooperation, free information flow, and decision-making that escapes top-down hierarchy, but with few exceptions the current state of DAOs does not deliver this. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
