   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6074",
   "text": "Blockchain presents the following source proposition: Cryptographic currencies like Bitcoin and others are among the most well-known blockchain applications, but there is a wide range of other uses that are as feasible. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Cryptographic hashing makes blockchain manipulation immediately detectable because the hash incorporates all previous transactions, so that even a single digit change produces a different hash value. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
