  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6069",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6069",
   "text": "Constructing Democratic Organizations with Digital Technology presents the following source proposition: It examines the shift from autocratic structures to more decentralized models, such as Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs), which promote participatory decision-making. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The authors stipulate that functioning democracies are decentralized autonomous organizations: the United States government is a DAO, as are Norway, Mauritius, Uruguay, and South Korea, and every functioning democracy is more akin to a DAO than to a centralized corporation. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-07-31",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
   "respondsTo": {
    "@id": "https://research.cbs.dk/en/publications/7e38d477-7cf9-4c1e-b1dc-32beed677bf8"
