   "text": "The Legal-Operational Interface of DAOs: A Governance Framework for Tokenized Adherence presents the following source proposition: Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs) pose a significant challenge to traditional legal frameworks. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Decentralized Autonomous Organizations challenge the core belief that governance necessitates agency, because a DAO can operate a governance structure built entirely on software, code, and smart contracts. The proposed response is a qualification: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
