   "text": "On the Integration of Artificial Intelligence and Blockchain Technology: A Perspective About Security presents the following source proposition: Whereas much research has been conducted on AI and Blockchain, there is a shortage of comprehensive studies examining their integration from a security perspective. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Private fund advisers' increasing use of blockchain technology, artificial intelligence, and big data is a distinct source of downward pressure on the traditional 2/20 fee structure that commentators have not examined. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
