  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6022",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6022",
   "text": "Governance of Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAO) and the Legal Nature of Smart Contracts presents the following source proposition: 이 글에서는 DAO가 무엇인지부터 시작해서 DAO의 장점과 단점, 법적 과제, 그리고 DAO의 몇 가지 예를 설명했다. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The immutability of blockchain ledgers is itself a vulnerability, because once a DAO is in operation its essential construction is very difficult to alter should a bug in the code appear. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
