  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-6019",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-6019",
   "text": "Decentralized autonomous organizations as an innovative form of economic cooperation in the digital society presents the following source proposition: Decentralized<br> autonomous organizations (DAOs) built on blockchain technology represent a new form of collective<br> management in which communities are organized based on the decentralized infrastructure of the third<br> generation of the Internet (Web 3.0). This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Decentralized Autonomous Organizations challenge the core belief that governance necessitates agency, because a DAO can operate a governance structure built entirely on software, code, and smart contracts. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
   "responseType": "extension",
   "datePublished": "2026-07-31",
   "creativeWorkStatus": "Affirmed",
