   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5999",
   "text": "Decentralized Autonomous Organizations and Organization Formation on Web3 presents the following source proposition: Chapter 9 offers a comprehensive exploration of decentralized autonomous organizations (DAOs) and their role in the formation of Web3 organizations. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Decentralized Autonomous Organizations have begun to challenge the core belief that governance necessitates agency, because blockchain enables the removal of agents as intermediaries through code, peer-to-peer connectivity, crowds, and collaboration. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
