  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-5995",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5995",
   "text": "Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs) in Cognitive IoT presents the following source proposition: It investigates how smart contracts and blockchain-based governance mechanisms enhance the autonomy, transparency, and efficiency of decision-making processes in IoT networks. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Without clear and effective governance mechanisms, DAO decision-making becomes slow and inefficient, delaying important changes and the resolution of internal issues. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
