  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-5985",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5985",
   "text": "The ConstitutionDAO: redefining crowdfunding in the age of decentralized finance presents the following source proposition: All references to individuals and events are based on verifiable public sources. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A decentralized autonomous organization is merely computer code with no directors, managers or employees, its governance structure built with software, code and smart contracts running on a public decentralized blockchain platform. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
