  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-5984",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5984",
   "text": "Regulation of Financial Protocol DAOs: Addressing the Problems of Decentralization and AI Governance presents the following source proposition: Additionally, the integration of artificial intelligence (AI) in DAOs introduces further complexities regarding accountability and liability, as AI lacks legal personhood. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that DAO-based governance introduces unresolved uncertainty about liability and legal accountability when personal data crosses international boundaries, and a mismatch between platform governance and regulatory mandates produces legal liability that erodes user trust. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
