   "text": "Enhancing Cyber-Physical-Social Systems through Decentralized Governance and Blockchain-based Digital Twins presents the following source proposition: However, the advancements enabled by Digital Twins (DTs), centralized governance models, and opaque analytics limit scalability and resilience. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The majority of private fund advisers that deploy blockchain technology, artificial intelligence, and big data in their operations or strategy charge their investors lower fees, even though not all blockchain enabled funds charge per transaction fees. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
