   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5959",
   "text": "Towards a Decentralized Autonomous Governance Model to Improve Governance of Charities presents the following source proposition: This systematic literature review (SLR) assesses the integration of DAO as a new way of managing charity projects through decentralized governance and smart contracts (SCs). This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A decentralized autonomous organization is merely computer code with no directors, managers or employees, its governance structure built with software, code and smart contracts running on a public decentralized blockchain platform. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
