   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5957",
   "text": "The Future of Decentralized Governance With DAO and Web 3 presents the following source proposition: Business logic and rules for running the organization are programmed in distributed applications (dApps) and executed using smart contracts. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A decentralized autonomous organization is merely computer code with no directors, managers or employees, its governance structure built with software, code and smart contracts running on a public decentralized blockchain platform. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
