  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-5955",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5955",
   "text": "DAOs vs. PBCs for Public Administration and Social Policy Entities presents the following source proposition: Legal identities are thus a fundamental characteristic of modern society. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Despite an early call for regulatory leadership from Commissioner Stein in 2015, the SEC has not addressed core recognition questions for blockchain in finance, including cryptocurrencies, tokens as securities, and DAOs as investment advisers. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
