   "evidenceLevel": "abstract indexed",
   "reviewTier": "moderate-confidence claim review",
   "mappingConfidence": 0.3511,
   "mappingAmbiguous": true
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-5951",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5951",
   "text": "Decentralized Organizations presents the following source proposition: It created a network-based ecosystem of participants who contributed computational power toward a singular goal. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A DAO realigns the otherwise disparate interests of principals and agents because all participants in the DAO share the same goal, which reduces behavior contrary to the interests of the organization. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
