   "text": "Decentralization as a new framework for the sharing economy presents the following source proposition: The ability to run smart contracts confers on blockchain technology the capability to run autonomous systems, from a simple transaction to an entire decentralized autonomous organization (DAO). This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A decentralized autonomous organization is merely computer code with no directors, managers or employees, its governance structure built with software, code and smart contracts running on a public decentralized blockchain platform. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
