  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-5892",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5892",
   "text": "Decision-making in Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs) presents the following source proposition: After an introduction to DAOs, describing basic elements and designs, the second part of this chapter will focus on governance aspects and describe how decision-making is implemented from the proposal process to voting and execution in DAOs. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The decentralized power structure is supposed to encourage cooperation, free information flow, and decision-making that escapes top-down hierarchy, but with few exceptions the current state of DAOs does not deliver this. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
