  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-5889",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5889",
   "text": "Experiments in algorithmic governance presents the following source proposition: In the original vision of decentralized autonomous organizations, as proposed by Vitalik Buterin, founder and member of the Ethereum Foundation, a DAO is a pseudo-legal organization run by an assemblage of human and “robot” participants. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A decentralized autonomous organization is merely computer code with no directors, managers or employees, its governance structure built with software, code and smart contracts running on a public decentralized blockchain platform. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
