  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-5888",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5888",
   "text": "Experiments in algorithmic governance presents the following source proposition: It details the governance structures that were promised by the developers and community members involved in the making of The decentralised autonomous organisation (DAO), and in contrast, those that were observed in its discourses before, during, and after the “exploit.” The DAO was a decentralized, crowdfunded, direct-management organization and investment platform. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A decentralized autonomous organization is merely computer code with no directors, managers or employees, its governance structure built with software, code and smart contracts running on a public decentralized blockchain platform. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
   "responseType": "extension",
