  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-5887",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5887",
   "text": "Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs) presents the following source proposition: But interestingly enough, there was a Web3 entity that entered the fray. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A jurisdiction is only truly favorable to DAOs if it grants the DAO limited liability as an entity and accepts its independent status without requiring any representative in that jurisdiction. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
