   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5885",
   "text": "Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs) presents the following source proposition: In November 2021, Sotheby’s auctioned a first edition copy of the US Constitution (there are only 13 in existence). This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A DAO needs a legal wrapper to represent it because a DAO on its own cannot rent an office or sign a contract that can only be executed on paper. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
