  },
  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-5883",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5883",
   "text": "DAO to (Anonymous) DAO Transactions presents the following source proposition: Blockchain assets are increasingly controlled by organizations rather than individuals. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Blockchain extends what the Internet did for information: it makes it possible to transfer and exchange value and assets without traditional centralized intermediaries, by storing information in a decentralized, accessible and secure online environment. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
