   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5828",
   "text": "Startups Without Founders: How Daos Redefine Entrepreneurship—A Systematic Review And Process Model For Decentralized Innovation presents the following source proposition: Focusing on Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs), we explore how startups can operate without a central leader, and what that means for the future of organizational design. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Decentralized Autonomous Organizations challenge the core belief that governance necessitates agency, attacking organizational design at a fundamental level rather than merely reforming it. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
