   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-5826",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5826",
   "text": "Blockweave: An Arweave‐Based Decentralized Storage Solution to Tackle the Blockchain Trilemma presents the following source proposition: Evaluation results show that Blockweave achieves the highest level of decentralization ( Tier‐S : 25,000 nodes with no entity controlling % of the network). This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Although blockchain technology itself offers unprecedented data and privacy protection, storing blockchain data across a global network of nodes often will not comply with the consumer protection rules, directives, and guidelines of particular jurisdictions. The proposed response is an agreement: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
