   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5814",
   "text": "A Review on the Security of the Ethereum-Based DeFi Ecosystem presents the following source proposition: It is based on blockchain technology and has attracted people’s attention because of its open, transparent, and intermediary free. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that In blockchain transactions the signing function, performed by wallets holding cryptographic keys, is separate from execution, which occurs inside the smart contract, so tokens are never physically held in the same locality as the keys and the smart contract acts as the intermediary executing predefined rules. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
