   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5812",
   "text": "Census of Decentralized Autonomous Organizations Across Platforms (2025) presents the following source proposition: This dataset provides a comprehensive, multi-platform overview of Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs) as of October 2025, covering DAO deployments, proposals, and voting activity across 6 major platforms: Aragon, DAOHaus, DAOstack, Realms, Snapshot and Tally. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that A decentralized autonomous organization is merely computer code with no directors, managers or employees, its governance structure built with software, code and smart contracts running on a public decentralized blockchain platform. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
