   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5805",
   "text": "Pathways to Performance: A Configurational Analysis of Consensus in DAOs presents the following source proposition: Our analysis challenges the notion of a single consensus model. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Tokens solve the quantification problem in quantum economics by serving as measurable units of value and governance: token denominated voting power in a DAO makes social influence and decision making power countable, supplying the consistent set of units the framework lacked. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
