   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5803",
   "text": "Pathways to Performance: A Configurational Analysis of Consensus in DAOs presents the following source proposition: Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs) represent a radical form of socio-technical systems, where rules are enforced by code and governance is conducted by a distributed network of stakeholders. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Each DAO in the dataset was given a score between zero and ten by the analyzing teams on each of six factors: Decentralization, Work to Earn, Attack Resistance, Regulatory Compliance, Governance, and Organizational Communication. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
