  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-5781",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5781",
   "text": "Decentralized, But Not Above the Law: Analyzing DAO Governance and Regulation presents the following source proposition: Decentralized autonomous organizations (DAOs) are transforming how people collaborate and manage collective ventures, yet the law has lagged behind this innovative form of organization. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Without a legal wrapper, DAOs face potential regulatory enforcement actions and civil liability not only at the organization level but against individual participants. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
