   "text": "Decentralized governance: empowering algorithms and autonomous organizations presents the following source proposition: It pays attention to DAO governance mechanisms and sheds light on eight well known mechanisms, such as token-based quorum voting, quadratic voting, and weighted voting. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that When only a minority of members, such as Audius node operators, can stake or earn weighted votes, the majority of token holders occupy the same powerless position as an ordinary shareholder in a corporation. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
