   "text": "Knowledge Compounding: An Empirical Economic Analysis of Self-Evolving Knowledge Wikis under the Agentic ROI Framework presents the following source proposition: (2026), this paper introduces knowledge compounding as a new measurable concept in the empirical economics of LLM agents and validates it through a controlled four-query experiment on Qing Claw, an industrial-grade C# reimplementation of the OpenClaw multi-agent framework. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Multi agent competitive collaboration captures a diversity dividend worth more than half a standard deviation of quality improvement while enabling attribution through citation graphs. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
