   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5759",
   "text": "Intelligence Cubed: A Decentralized Modelverse for Democratizing AI presents the following source proposition: The rapid advancement of artificial intelligence (AI) has been largely characterized by centralized development and control, limiting accessibility and innovation. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that Private fund advisers' increasing use of blockchain technology, artificial intelligence, and big data is a distinct source of downward pressure on the traditional 2/20 fee structure that commentators have not examined. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
