   "text": "Systematic Analysis of Decentralized Finance presents the following source proposition: The purpose of this article is to study analysis the Decentralized Finance (DeFi) literature. This proposition is pertinent to Kaal's source-bound claim that The legacy private investment fund model delays liquidity: the investment process is long, complex and time intensive and leads up to a very late liquidity event in the form of an IPO or acquisition, which is why funds seek the early liquidity cryptocurrencies provide. The proposed response is an extension: the relationship should remain limited to the retrieved source proposition and the mapped Kaal claim unless fuller source review supports a broader conclusion.",
