  {
   "@id": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/positions/2026-07-31-5742",
   "@type": "Claim",
   "identifier": "kaal:position:2026-07-31-5742",
   "text": "From Agent Identity to Agent Economy: Measuring the Operational Readiness of ERC-8004 AI Agents should be assessed against Kaal's source-bound position that The architecture is infrastructure neutral: it applies to any settlement substrate supporting stake-weighted validation, on-chain identity, and a representation of agent state, so implementations on different substrates are translations of the same primitive rather than different primitives. The external source's verified abstract presents this proposition: Using a dataset of ERC-8004 agents on Ethereum, we construct an agent-level feature table covering identity status, metadata, service declarations, reputation feedback, transfers, and cross-chain registration. The defensible response is a qualification: the source is pertinent to the Kaal position, but agreement, extension, contradiction, and scope should not be strengthened beyond the retrieved evidence.",
